+| Pending assistant response | Show a three-dot pending indicator on Daylight's side after deliberate submission, replacing the bottom thinking text. Use staggered spatial wave motion so waiting is visibly active, with static reduced-motion dots. Expose one meaningful accessible status and avoid repeated announcements. Clear the indicator on success, recovery or cancellation; it does not imply unchecked text is ready to display. | Pending/success/error/cancel transitions, spatial animation, accessibility and reduced-motion checks; no additional model request. |
+| Growing composer | Give the composer more initial room and let its height follow the draft within usable bounds. Reserve that space so the conversation reading pane moves up rather than being covered. Keep Send, focus, draft and local reading/scroll behavior usable, including phone keyboards. | Short/long drafts, resize/keyboard and desktop/tablet/phone checks; no transcript replay or lost draft. |
+| Draft and reading continuity | Unsent text stays in place while choosing, opening utilities or returning. Transcript scrolling/focus stays local to the reading pane. | Browser draft and return checks; preserve existing handlers. |
+| Submitted draft lifecycle | Clear submitted composer text immediately when Send begins, and shrink its height accordingly. Retain the submitted text privately for recovery; restore after failure only if there is no newer draft to overwrite. Pending, success, failure, cancellation and replay must not discard a newer draft or submit twice. | Immediate-clear, failure restoration, newer-draft preservation, composer shrink and cancellation/replay tests; no transcript or draft persistence expansion. |
+| Content below the viewport | Offer a labeled downward jump control only when useful later conversation content is out of view. Hide it when caught up, keep it above the composer and preserve keyboard focus/local reading behavior. Automatic scrolling must not pull a reader away from older text. | Hidden/visible states after scroll, reveal and resize; click/keyboard operation; desktop/tablet/phone and reduced-motion checks. |
+| Nonblocking recovery | Invalid generated prose stays out of history. One status notice leaves the service-approved post-capture question/choices available; never invent an answered question or present an educational pause as completion. Repeated failures do not accumulate generic chat paragraphs. Use one accessible status live region. | Controller recovery, repeated-failure renderer/Send tests and real browser check. |
+| Current natural flow | Clear reports consolidate without routine acceptance cards; ambiguity and named actions keep their distinct checks. Profile review remains optional at the end; corrections during intake can be typed. No Back, Review or Prepare controls clutter the intake footer. | Natural-flow regression suite. |
+| Education and practical progress | After substantial teaching, the advisor may offer up to two short contextual educational follow-up questions while retaining one consequential practical question and its return point. Suggestions fill the existing composer for review and deliberate Send, transfer nothing on selection and must not overwrite an existing draft. Skip unnecessary suggestions after short answers; never require an education detour, create a lesson queue or infer comprehension/preference from interaction. User-led side questions can continue before returning to the pending practical question. | Suggested-question scope/count, grounded relevance, no-auto-Send/no-draft-overwrite, preserved pending-question context and short-response omission tests; conversation/comprehension evaluation remains separate. |
+| Narrative alignment | Current topic may move between circumstances, reviewed teaching and options without implying intake completion. Newcomer insurance groups refine locally to the exact approved answer before capture. One deliberate finite-answer Send may use v2 context for composition only; choosing/refining never transfers. Explicit changed priorities retain only bounded, scoped reasons tied to the current report revision; reading alone records no agreement or understanding. | Focus, choice refinement, Send parity, agenda revision and privacy tests. |
+| Contextual visual guide and Sources | Show a compact inline visual only when it supports the current explanation; historical topic exposure does not keep an old guide visible. The guide and coverage paths read coherently without a dropdown. Sources remains a native expandable, inspectable footer; combine and de-duplicate current reply/guide sources so it appears once after the guide. Viewing a visual/source does not establish comprehension, preference or verified personal coverage. | Current-turn relevance/absence, ordinary follow-up and educational-turn checks; source expansion and retained history behavior. |
+| Existing visual identity | Keep the accepted layout, type, progress, photo and composer. The latest owner direction removes premature default references and reduces intake utilities to privacy. Keep :8891 itself protected. | Static/style hashes and responsive browser inspection. |
+
+Before an interface change, identify the intended difference and compare it with this table. Run the normal Python suite, which includes the Node renderer interaction tests, and inspect the affected behavior in the browser. If a behavior must be removed, record that owner decision before deleting it; do not infer removal from a new narrative or backend plan.
+
+These checks reduce known regressions; they do not claim every historic feature has been inventoried or that automated tests replace owner review. The first protected regression is the assistant reveal that layout/backend-only checks missed. Add observed interaction failures here with behavioral tests.
+
+The October 30 contextual-conversation correction explicitly changes the earlier inline-form and footer baseline. Recent dialogue uses v2 permission and server-only bounded visit memory; v1 remains profile-only. Future changes must preserve this corrected baseline, not restore the superseded form controls.
+
+The October 31 owner direction preserves the visual shell while authorizing the narrative-alignment behavior above. Topic labels replace the fixed phase labels only on :8893, retaining the compact treatment. Recommendations and new research capabilities are outside this change.
