+# Daylight advisor-first local variant
+
+**November 2 COBRA correction · locally active:** Relative start preferences and partial reported end dates are retained; COBRA questions use the correct insurance scope. Official timing teaching comes before demanding a calendar preference. [Verification and remaining model limits](../../audit-evidence/advisor-cobra-recovery-20261102/README.md).
+
+**D86 conversation quality · November 2 · implemented and locally active.** Current-decision guidance ranks the existing eligible questions without forcing an intake sequence. Education can take a detour or end without a question; the practical return point stays available. Current clarification and new supported aspects can deepen teaching, while bounded claim and question guards protect report/evidence meaning. Helper learning never becomes a beneficiary fact or priority. The accepted frontend, existing two-stage model flow, v3 visit-only context, saving/budget controls and all research/recommendation holds remain. [Current execution evidence](../../audit-evidence/advisor-conversation-quality-20261102/README.md) distinguishes regression tests, actual fictional live attempts and costs, limited responsive entry inspection, independent review, runtime activation and remaining quality limits. Refresh and start a fresh visit after the :8893 restart. The final live journey did not pass its quality rubric; the subsequent explicit-stop recovery fix has regression coverage. Earlier packet totals below are historical builds.
+
+**D86 adaptive curriculum · November 2 · implemented and active.** A 17-concept visit learning record now accompanies the reported profile, separating introduced/explored/open clarification from comprehension. The model receives that history; citations, actual teaching and visual intent are separate. Ordinary answers advance without repeated introductions, while requested recaps and educational detours preserve the practical return point. The existing UI/styles/model/stage count/budget remain. Token compaction and bounded packing, generic-teaching validation and a narrow caregiver relationship fix address defects found during verification. The final suite passes 712 tests; all 30 personas retain 2,164 passing assertions. Targeted real-model checks and continuations cost $0.4126365 measured plus a $0.0335 unresolved hold. Learning stays in permissioned visit RAM, outside saved profiles. The [contract](../../docs/product/ADAPTIVE_CURRICULUM_2026-11-02.md) and [evidence](../../audit-evidence/advisor-curriculum-20261102/README.md) distinguish actual live coverage, remaining limits and local activation. Refresh and start a fresh visit after the :8893 restart; saved profiles and protected variants remain unchanged.
+
