+
+## Operate locally
+
+Check the job:
+
+```sh
+launchctl print gui/501/com.daylight.advisor-first.8893
+```
+
+After an authorized source change, restart only this variant:
+
+```sh
+launchctl kickstart -k gui/501/com.daylight.advisor-first.8893
+```
+
+Stop without deleting any records:
+
+```sh
+launchctl bootout gui/501/com.daylight.advisor-first.8893
+```
+
+Start it again from this folder:
+
+```sh
+launchctl bootstrap gui/501 "$PWD/runtime/com.daylight.advisor-first.8893.plist"
+```
+
+The checked-in local plist uses `../../infrastructure/daylight-data/.venv/bin/python`, `--local-research` and explicit `--identity-research`; the dependency is `psycopg`, already installed locally. The service binds only to loopback. The exact private PostgreSQL cluster and selected source/build receipts must pass their existing ownership/read-only checks. `--local-research` constructs the original accepted-reference adapter; `--identity-research` separately enables trusted internal source-identity inspection, with all consumer purposes held. Omitting either flag disables its corresponding connection without changing source acceptance. The plist and local physical-target guard are not portable cloud configuration: hosting requires a separately bound target, roles, secrets, network/pooling and backup/restore checks. Do not restart other Daylight jobs, restore their databases or reset the shared ledger as part of this variant's rollback.
+
+When changing launch arguments, `kickstart` does not reread the plist. Use the documented separate bootout/bootstrap steps, confirm the old process exited, and check the new job and API afterward. This work's initial immediate bootstrap returned macOS error 5; the original service was recovered, then the updated configuration started successfully in separate steps. Exact attempts and successful checks are retained in the evidence packet.
+
+## Development and verification
+
+Controlled tests use temporary private databases and synthetic model outputs, with no paid generation:
+
+```sh
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m unittest discover -s alternatives/advisor-first/tests -v
+node --check alternatives/advisor-first/web/advisor.js
+```
+
+For a disposable UI preview, run from this folder with an unused fixture port and temporary database:
+
+```sh
+fixture_dir=$(mktemp -d /tmp/daylight-advisor-fixture.XXXXXX)
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 server.py --fixture --port 8892 --database "$fixture_dir/guides.sqlite3"
+```
+
+The fixture explicitly labels mocked replies and does not certify language-model behavior. [Delivery evidence](../../audit-evidence/advisor-first-20261030/README.md) records controlled tests, actual live AI checks, responsive walkthroughs and preservation checks separately.
+
+## Boundaries
+
+- The original 41 reviewed IDs, 78 field records, 14 additive report paths and 14 gaps remain traceable. They are conditional dependencies, not a mandatory questionnaire.
+- The model generates grounded prose and question wording within service-owned eligible moves, resolved report references and reviewed teaching. It cannot bypass missing dependencies, rank plans or expand permissions. The current supported operation is education/preparation; research/recommendation capabilities remain held.
+- Messages and drafts are visit-only. Saving uses the existing opt-in policy with a separate sensitive-detail choice, seven-day guest scope, same-browser resume and explicit deletion. Prior relevant details require the versioned AI-context permission; raw history is not attached. New report confirmations are stored as reported, rather than falsely claiming a user approved a summary.
+- Reviews expire after ten minutes and are bound to the owner and exact input snapshot. An edit invalidates the affected confirmation. Operation keys prevent duplicate preparation execution. Edited checklist versions remain available in the current visit under Review information.
+- The approved $5/UTC-day allowance for :8893, shared accounting, model/pricing review, bounded token limits and no automatic AI retries remain. The UI does not display consumer spend banners.
+- Sample browsing remains five unvalidated **2027 Collier County** records. Reported 2026 timing is not silently replaced, and no sample establishes personal fit or complete coverage.
+- All source/eligibility/provider/drug/price/Medigap/recommendation/enrollment holds, commercial independence and sealed evidence obligations remain intact. A preparation receipt is not an outside verification or a sent request.
+- Physical mobile keyboards, assistive-technology execution and observed consumer comprehension/A/B/C comparisons remain separate validation work. No confidence, savings or superiority claim is made from technical tests.
