+      "trigger": "First classify explicit existing insurance-ending/move/plan/program facts from T04/T05/chat and move/end-date reports. At a requested check that still needs an unresolved event fact, name the precise insurance/location/program event and purpose in a targeted follow-up. No broad What changed about your coverage/needs question or routine event menu. Intent to enroll/change is already task context, not a qualifying event; care-needs/preferences changes use their existing branches. If a reviewed route and known facts already resolve the requested timing, skip event discovery. Missing sources or inventory order cannot trigger it.",
+      "acceptable_evidence_or_confirmation": "Explicit relevant past/upcoming event report, selection or minimal notice summary tied to beneficiary, affected insurance/program/location and period/provenance. Reuse an unambiguous account without another menu. Retirement alone does not establish insurance ending: clarify only that consequential relation when missing. Another event needs only consequential missing meaning; intent to re-enroll and help exposure supply no event fact.",
+      "unknown_conflict_handling": "Explicit no-change-to-report differs from unknown/deferred; silence is neither. A reported event is not an enrollment-right finding, and no reported event is not proof that no other enrollment route exists or that Medicare must be re-enrolled annually. Preserve multiple/unlisted events and each binding; the single choice is an explicit representation limitation if it cannot express them. Confirm consequential same-event conflicts without erasing known facts or forcing a closest category. Contextual Why does this matter / Help me find the details can return to still-unknown without a quiz or retry.",
