+      "trigger": "Before an ask, identify the beneficiary's specific job-linked insurance from a prior T05/chat report, the requested timing/coordination conclusion and the exact missing worker/current-work distinction. Name that insurance/relationship in the follow-up; an unanchored this coverage fails the trigger. T05 retiree/COBRA and clear own/spouse/family current-job reports already supply their classification. If only whose job remains consequential, ask only that; if only current versus former work remains, ask only that. Place beside the relevant T05 answer or later explicit work-related timing task, never as a new topic after RC08. Explicit absence closes the branch; unknown T05 does not silently become no job coverage. Unrelated learning/doctor/drug work, inventory order and source gaps cannot trigger it.",
+      "acceptable_evidence_or_confirmation": "Explicit own/spouse/family current-job, retiree or COBRA report/selection or relevant benefits-administrator/notice summary, tied to beneficiary, actual job providing this insurance, policy/period and provenance. Reuse a clear T05 retiree/COBRA or current-job/source report without another menu/confirmation turn. If kind is known, ask only whose job; if the worker is known, ask only current-work status. Confirm consequential interpretation of vague employer coverage, not every literal report.",
+      "unknown_conflict_handling": "Unknown/deferred is not retired, COBRA or active employment. Employer/carrier name, who pays premiums, beneficiary retirement or caregiver role does not establish the insured worker/current-work relationship. The relevant worker may have a different current job from the one providing this coverage. Preserve multiple job-linked policies and their periods; a single choice cannot encode them all. A broad family-member label is insufficient when the reviewed rule needs the exact relationship: retain the explicit report/binding gap and ask only that necessary detail. No auto-classification from the beneficiary being retired, and no unchanged-unknown retry.",
+      "source_data_layer": "Existing customer-profile report/confirmation provenance; L13 enrollment/coordination. Official enrollment/administrator notices and reviewed rule versions are separate from a user report. This describes required evidence, not independent acceptance. Exact benefits-administrator/employment/plan-period evidence must support the rule in use; own/spouse/other-family cases are not assumed interchangeable. Medicare.gov Working past 65, checked October 27, supports the general distinction between current-employment and retiree/COBRA coverage for Part B timing, not this person's eligibility or independent L13 acceptance. G04/G13 policy/partial-classification and G10 basis-specific coordination gaps remain explicit. Optional conceptual/practical help is education, not verified employment or enrollment.",
