+      "requirement": "Conditional internal missing-fact check only when an actual requested Part D enrollment/deferral/continuity finding or contemplated coverage action needs other prescription-insurance creditability not already established. No routine notice request for other insurance, retirement, browsing, medicine/formulary/price checks or RC11 completion. Applicability belongs to the system, not the user; branch frequency is unmeasured.",
+      "trigger": "Identify the beneficiary, named other prescription plan/program, relevant period and concrete consequence from T01/T04/T05/chat (RC09/RC26 only if needed). An explicit penalty question is unnecessary if a contemplated deferral/transition itself needs the check. Reuse an adequately bound notice/program determination/report first. Only then explain why and ask what the named employer/plan told the person, with optional practical/terminology help. Owner explicitly removed the as-good-as-Medicare-standard comparison from proposed consumer wording; never ask them to judge benefit equivalence or require comprehension of that standard. Explicit no drug insurance skips the notice question; history is independently conditional.",
+      "acceptable_evidence_or_confirmation": "Explicit positive/negative notice wording or user report of a relevant employer/plan/program determination, with issuer, exact coverage/period and provenance. Reuse a current sufficiently scoped fact without another selection. Ask for only relevant wording/effective period, not member numbers/full documents. Current notice alone proves neither past-year status nor actual continuous enrollment. Exact accepted program evidence can support the fact only with a valid beneficiary/program/period binding.",
