+      "requirement": "Conditional internal intention/scope check consolidated with the existing goal/current-coverage conversation. Suppress a routine replacement yes/no ask. Exploring options or remaining undecided does not block useful comparison or require a replacement commitment.",
+      "trigger": "An actual current Medigap policy and requested work make the target policy/intention consequential, but exact supported prior goal reports do not already establish it. Reuse T01/T05/RC15/chat before asking. Clarify only an ambiguity that would change the next useful review, cause unnecessary intake or affect an actual replacement-specific finding. A vague request with known supplement and drug policies may justify asking which coverage to review; do not force a keep/replace decision merely to fill the field. RC16 completion, a price preference or Medigap history alone is insufficient.",
+      "acceptable_evidence_or_confirmation": "Explicit goal for the named current policy, including a clear request to compare alternatives, an expressed intent to retain/change or an explicit undecided response; preserve person, policy, period, source/confirmation/revision. Reuse unambiguous free text without redundant confirmation. Comparing premiums is an exploration report, not commitment or permission to cancel. No policy documents, member numbers, health history or full finances are needed solely for intention. Actual existing-policy status/rights/evidence remain separate.",
+      "unknown_conflict_handling": "Unknown/undecided is never keep or replace by default. Preserve exploring, decided intent, retaining, considering leaving without another Medigap policy and explicit limits as distinct meanings. The two original options cannot faithfully encode them all; keep the raw report and explicit representation gap rather than forcing a closest legacy value. Current Medigap versus separate Part D or other insurance must be identified from known facts, not inferred from the word plan. A historical policy is not an existing one; an intention is not an executed cancellation. Reconcile material contradictions with the person rather than last-report overwrite.",
