+## T05 · Current coverage · wording/multi-select/presented use rules approved
+
+**Existing wording:** What health coverage do you have now?
+
+**Proposed short rationale:** “This helps us understand what you might keep or change, and what needs checking first.”
+
+**Existing inline options, select all that apply:** Original Medicare (Parts A and B) · Medicare Advantage (Part C) · Medicare Supplement / Medigap · Separate prescription drug plan · Current-job coverage · Retiree coverage · COBRA · VA, TRICARE or military coverage · Medicaid · None · Not sure.
+
+**Response/conversation proposal:** Keep the question and existing multi-select options. For a helper, ask about the established beneficiary's coverage, not the helper's. Reuse clear confirmed reports rather than showing the full list again. A free-text reply can supply several explicit coverage categories and relevant later facts; confirm consequential interpretations and do not force the person to translate a carrier name into an insurance category. A carrier name or the word “Medicare” alone may need clarification rather than automatic classification. Existing choices are retained for review; any coverage that does not fit them must remain an explicit unresolved representation gap, not be relabeled None or invented as an active supported enum.
+
+**Single existing field:** `guide.fields.coverage.current` contains the reported category set. It does not by itself contain exact policy identifiers, verified enrollment or benefit evidence. The record below names all seven required mapping dimensions for this field.
+
+| Field | Decision affected | Mandatory / conditional / optional | Trigger | Acceptable evidence / confirmation | Unknown / conflict handling | Source / data layer | Readiness gate |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `guide.fields.coverage.current` | Reported current-coverage baseline for comparing keep/change paths; which employment, drug-coverage, military, assistance, Medigap or transition checks are consequential. Category selection alone does not settle those checks or identify the exact policies. | Conditional: mandatory for a personal keep/change, coordination or timing conclusion that depends on current coverage. Not required for general Medicare learning or a published availability check that does not depend on current coverage. | Requested task needs the current coverage baseline, but categories for the same beneficiary/current period are missing, stale, ambiguous or conflicting. Reuse clear confirmed categories already supplied; ask only for missing consequential distinctions. | Explicit multi-select report or sufficiently specific confirmed user statement, linked to T05 or the original known-fact report with beneficiary, period, provenance and confirmation retained. One reply can supply several categories. Category-level reports can support preparation; verified enrollment, benefits or continuity claims require the relevant official/program/carrier evidence separately. Do not request government ID numbers to establish a category. | Silence is unanswered, never None. Explicit None and Not sure are different and are exclusive global choices in the existing control. Preserve known categories when only a later detail is unknown; do not replace the entire baseline with unknown. Do not auto-correct apparently incompatible same-person/same-period Original/Advantage reports; clarify through RC07/RC28, including whether they refer to different periods. Unsupported coverage types remain explicit gaps rather than forced categories. Allow correction, preserve prior reports, and invalidate only affected dependent conclusions. | User-reported customer-profile field; existing T05 map/contract or a specific already-known fact. When used, exact published evidence may come from L01