+
+### Existing conditional prompts and duplicate-ask prevention
+
+- **RC04 / RC07:** Reuse explicit statements about current parts and Original/Advantage delivery from the same confirmed reply. “I have Medicare” or a carrier name cannot silently establish both. Store each supported fact under its existing field rather than requiring a duplicate consumer question. Reported status remains distinct from official enrollment evidence.
+- **RC09–RC14:** Employment/retiree/COBRA reports can open only the consequential remaining employment relationship, end dates, creditable-drug notice/gap, household-impact or HSA details. Do not ask every employment question merely because one category was selected.
+- **RC15–RC17:** Medigap or Advantage history matters only for the requested rights/change check; current category alone does not establish history or buying rights.
+- **RC18 / RC19:** A Medicaid report or assistance-related task can make exact relevant assistance/qualification facts consequential. Do not infer a particular subsidy, qualification or amount from the broad Medicaid category.
+- **RC26:** Ask the exact military/veterans program only when consequential and not already explicitly identified. The broad military option is not evidence that all such programs apply.
+- **RC28:** Resolve consequential conflicts while retaining original reports. Different current versus future periods are not automatically a contradiction.
+
+**Example:** “I have Original Medicare, a Medigap policy and a separate drug plan” can supply three current-coverage categories in one reply. It supplies no policy identifier, exact premium, network participation or formulary confirmation. Reuse clear parts/delivery claims where supported rather than asking them again.
+
+### Explicit representation and evidence gaps to resolve
+
+The existing category field and the active 78-path template do not provide a dedicated exact-current-policy-identity field. A concrete keep-current-policy versus switch comparison may need the relevant policy/program name, exact plan/product identity and applicable year/period, together with actual benefit/cost evidence. This fact is linked to **T05 or a specific already-known policy fact**; its active schema representation and any consequential missing-detail wording remain unresolved. It must not be invented from a carrier or category, silently defaulted to a sample, or treated as satisfied by finishing T05. Until the gap is resolved, withhold that exact-policy baseline conclusion. This does not add another primary question or activate legacy fields.
+
+The present option list also lacks an explicit Other coverage category. If the person describes other coverage, preserve the original meaning under the existing privacy rules and mark classification/representation unresolved. A future Other/free-text storage extension is a review decision, not something this document claims is implemented. This limitation does not justify dropping the reported coverage, classifying it as None, or making an unsupported change recommendation.
+
+**Owner decision, October 25:** Chris replied “yes, continue” to keeping the question, multi-select choices and conditional/reuse rules. The presented product rules are approved. The exact-current-policy and Other-coverage representation gaps remain unresolved rather than silently filled or removed by that agreement. No runtime or independent policy/source acceptance follows from this review decision.
