+## T06 · Providers to check · free text and identity echo owner-directed
+
+**Existing wording:** Which doctors or hospitals would you like to keep?
+
+**Proposed short rationale:** “This helps us identify the provider access that needs checking.”
+
+**Revised answer mode, directed by Chris:** Begin with free text. The earlier Add doctors or hospitals / None to check / Add later option-first presentation is superseded in this reviewed design. The person can type several names and any practice/town they know in one reply, or say none, later or “I don't know.” Reuse existing sufficiently specific reports. For a helper, use the established beneficiary's providers. General learning does not require a provider inventory.
+
+**Provider-identity echo:** Match each entered doctor/hospital against the available provider inventory being assembled, then show relevant candidate identities for the person to confirm. Display full name, practice and office location; use specialty/address when needed to distinguish candidates. An inventory candidate is not selected, confirmed or marked covered merely because it is the closest result. Do not imply that the full provider inventory, matching adapter or network verification is already complete or accepted. Keep inventory scope/source/freshness and missing matches explicit.
+
+**Proposed confirmation flow:** One reply can produce one compact grouped echo of all named providers. Clearly distinguish candidate matches from identity matches the user has confirmed. Offer explicit confirmation/correction and a way to choose another match, say not listed, or leave an item unsure. If several identities remain plausible, show the relevant candidates for that item without preselection. Ask only for missing distinguishing information; do not require practice/location text again after the person confirms the exact office record. Confirm several unambiguous new matches together when useful, while keeping unresolved items independent. Reuse an already confirmed current identity unless the relevant details have changed.
+
+**Autocomplete:** Optional future interaction enhancement. The baseline design accepts the full free-text reply, retrieves candidate matches and then asks for confirmation. Search-as-you-type is not required by this decision. Any candidate matching/order uses relevant name/location identity evidence, independently of commissions or carrier relationships; it is not a plan recommendation.
+
+**Two existing fields:** `guide.fields.needs.providersStatus` records whether there are named providers to investigate, explicitly none requested, or an unresolved/deferred scope. `guide.fields.needs.providers` retains the reported names/list. Neither is independent identity or access verification.
