+## RC13 · Effect of a proposed change on existing group benefits · conditional use approved
+
+**Original inventory question:** Could a change affect anyone else’s coverage?
+
+**Original options:** Administrator says yes · Administrator says no · I have not checked.
+
+**What it uncovers:** Whether the specific contemplated action would change existing employer/union/retiree benefits for the person or connected people. RC12's creditability answer does not establish these consequences. [Official Medicare guidance](https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/part-d/basics/creditable-coverage), checked October 27, identifies possible effects on the person's, spouse's or dependents' employer/union coverage when adding Medicare drug coverage. The actual plan's terms/administrator must establish the applicable effect; this is no personal coverage determination or source acceptance.
