+**Revised plain-language example, when wife/work-plan departure is already known:** What has your employer told you happens to your wife's insurance if you leave the work plan for Medicare?
+
+**Example responses for that context:** She can keep it · It would end or change · I haven't checked · I don't know. These are scoped reported outcomes for the wife, not a finding that every other benefit stays unchanged. Preserve known partial/mixed effects and ask for detail only when the requested decision needs it.
+
+**Revised contextual question for the existing husband/add-drug-coverage flow below:** Has his employer said whether both of you can keep your work insurance if you add Medicare drug coverage?
+
+**Short examples for explanation/help:** Your wife or child gets insurance through your job and you are considering leaving that work plan for Medicare: check whether their insurance continues. Or you are on your husband's work insurance and want to add Medicare drug coverage: check whether his plan would keep covering both of you. These are illustrative, plan-specific questions, not statements that Medicare enrollment automatically ends anyone's insurance. Use only the relevant example inline; do not make users answer an examples menu or collect family names/ages solely to explain this purpose. The person's own relevant retiree/group benefits remain in scope even if nobody else is covered.
