+**Critique:** Yes/No answers only the first clause; the question bundles three facts and lacks an unknown response. First-ever Advantage entry, start of the relevant enrollment and former Medigap history are distinct. Different federal protections have different history requirements, so no automatic three-question sequence follows. The official guide distinguishes joining when first eligible for Part A at 65 from dropping Medigap to try Advantage for the first time; current age or a recent plan start alone establishes neither route. G01 explicitly retains the missing first-eligibility/history anchor when needed, without a new primary prompt.
