+## RC20 · Away-care details · T08 consolidation/missing-details-only use approved
+
+**Necessity assessment first:** Consolidate RC20 with T08 and existing intended-provider/chat reports; suppress a second broad travel question/menu. T08 can already supply the care kind and coarse destination, and a free-text reply can supply both detail fields. Only a specific supported access/travel result needing a missing place or care distinction earns a follow-up. General education/path comparison may need no city or personal itinerary. The original options mix geography with emergency-only need, omit same-state away care and unknown, and cannot represent multiple places/needs. Preserve the owner-approved broader U.S. scope rather than restoring another-state-only routing. A source outage is an external hold, not a reason to re-ask travel facts.
+
+**Original inventory question:** Where will you need routine care away from home?
+
+**Original options:** Another U.S. state · Outside the U.S. · Emergency travel cover only.
+
+**What it uncovers:** Which care the person wants away from home and where, to the extent those facts change the requested access check. Emergency benefits do not establish access to planned appointments. Never make the person choose one of U.S., overseas or emergency-only as though those are mutually exclusive dimensions.
+
+**Prior-answer flow (illustrative, not actual customer facts):** T08/chat says I need regular checkups while I'm in Arizona each winter. Planned-care meaning and the state are already known. If the requested provider/network check genuinely needs the city and it has not been supplied, ask only:
+
+**Proposed contextual question:** Which city in Arizona should we check for doctor visits?
+
+**Response:** Free text, with I don't know / I haven't decided available. Accept several cities or a named intended office in one reply and reuse any existing intended-provider location. A date/duration question earns a place only if a specific source-supported condition actually uses that fact; there is no default travel calendar or lodging-address collection.
+
+**Zero-ask flow:** I spend winters in Phoenix and want to keep seeing my doctor there for scheduled appointments supplies care meaning and destination. Reuse them; T06/RC21 handles any genuinely missing provider identity separately. Do not repeat T08, ask which state or reinterpret Phoenix as the permanent home. Several intended locations stay separate with their own needs/periods.
+
+**Only if care kind is genuinely unclear:** If the person merely mentions travel and the actual check needs planned-care intent, a short targeted ask is Will you need regular doctor visits while you're in [place]? Yes / No / I don't know. No planned visits is not a fabricated emergency-only report or a verified coverage finding. An already clear T08 routine-care answer skips this entirely. These are independently conditional uses of the existing fields, not an automatic sequence after every travel answer.
