+## RC22 · Exact medicine product detail · T07 consolidation approved
+
+**Necessity assessment first:** Consolidate with T07; suppress a blanket exact-name/strength/form/preference questionnaire and Add details gate. Reuse the current reported list, label details and explicitly confirmed product matches. Ask only genuinely missing product distinctions needed by the requested supported coverage/price check. Generic education or a source-supported broad statement need not earn an exact-product interview. If several missing label details are needed, collect them naturally together rather than serializing the six fields into six questions. A failed identity/formulary source is an external hold, not a reason to repeat known label details.
+
+**Critical distinction:** Actual branded/generic product identity may be essential; optional brand/generic preference is a different fact. Preserve the actual product in name/product binding even when preference is unasked. Never treat a reported brand as loyalty, assume generic acceptable or interpret a preference as permission to substitute medicines. Strength is a product attribute, not dosing instructions; fill quantity/days supply/pharmacy belong only to the actually needed RC23 pricing scenario. Form/release/route/concentration/device factors are collected only at the precision an exact supported product check needs. Clinical changes and diagnosis are not inferred.
+
+**Original inventory question:** What exact name, strength, form, and brand or generic preference should we use for each medicine?
+
+**Original options:** Add exact name, strength and form · No longer taking.
+
+**Prior-answer flow (synthetic, no live match or customer facts):** T07 says Naproxen. If an actual supported product check needs still-missing label strength/form after prior facts are reused, ask:
