+## RC23 · Fill amount, supply and pharmacy · Conditional missing-detail use approved
+
+**Necessity assessment first:** Keep RC23 conditional at the actual requested fill-price check, consolidated with T07/RC22 reports; suppress the broad for-each-medicine question and Add supply menu. A pharmacy-independent formulary listing needs no full refill interview. Ask only the missing amount, days or store/service distinction required by a supported result; one reply/compact inline group can supply several. Quantity and pharmacy can also matter to an explicitly requested quantity-limit or pharmacy-network finding: reuse just those relevant facts, rather than falsely declaring all fill details pricing-only. This narrower dependency/capability-metadata gap is explicit in G05; it changes no runtime policy or accepted source scope. If only an unsupported pricing adapter/source/model is missing, defer personal collection and explain the limit.
+
+**Original inventory question:** For each medicine, what quantity, days supply, exact pharmacy and retail or mail order should we use?
+
+**Original options:** Add supply and pharmacy · Mail order.
+
+**Problems with the original:** A details-selection gate supplies no actual fill facts. Mail order is one answer dimension, not an alternative to knowing amount/days/exact service. The question bundles internal terminology, and a universal per-medicine interview repeats supplied facts. Quantity, strength and days supply are different. A 90-day refill does not automatically mean mail order, and delivery alone does not establish a plan's mail-order service. Keep actual reported use and an explicitly requested hypothetical comparison separate; never replace one with a source-supported alternative silently.
+
+**Owner-approved conditional dropdown/missing-detail approach; detailed design:** Use persistent plain labels, no preselection and keyboard/assistive-technology-accessible native or equivalent controls. T07 remains free text; these are missing-detail follow-ups, not a new questionnaire. Known confirmed values are reused with correction available, not shown as unanswered dropdowns. A newly extracted ambiguous interpretation remains a candidate until consequential confirmation. Every requested input supports I don't know and defer; source failure has its own state.
