+## RC26 · Military/veterans program identity · Conditional T05 use approved
+
+**Necessity assessment first:** Keep as a conditional missing-program clarification within T05/current-coverage chat. Ask only when identifying the program at the necessary precision changes a supported requested enrollment/coordination/drug/path conclusion and prior reports do not already supply it. The broad VA/TRICARE/military category is insufficient for some rules; no universal second program question follows from selecting it. General education may need no subtype. A specific current program report is reused without echoing known facts. Serving in the military, receiving a non-health VA benefit or describing a spouse's program does not establish current beneficiary health coverage. Missing source/policy verification is an external hold, not another personal question.
+
+**Concrete reason it can matter:** [TRICARE's TFL eligibility FAQ](https://tricare.mil/FAQs/TFL/TFL_Eligibility), checked October 27, requires TRICARE eligibility and Medicare A/B, while noting active-duty exceptions to transitioning to TFL. [VA health-care/other-insurance guidance](https://www.va.gov/resources/va-health-care-and-other-insurance/) describes a distinct VA/Medicare arrangement, not a single generic military policy. [CHAMPVA guidance](https://www.va.gov/family-and-caregiver-benefits/health-and-disability/champva/) has its own program/Medicare requirements. Thus a generic military answer cannot support a personal keep/drop/defer/coordination conclusion. These are examples of why exact rules matter, not verified individual eligibility or a new accepted policy module. Program name alone does not settle basis, status, exceptions, periods or costs.
+
+**Original inventory question:** Which military or veterans’ coverage do you have?
+
+**Original options:** VA health care · TRICARE For Life · Other TRICARE · CHAMPVA · Another program.
+
+**Proposed treatment and controls:** Retain the original plain question when the broad category remains the actual consequential unknown. Present an unselected dropdown supporting multiple applicable reports, with the original program names, typed Another program and I'm not sure. Add How can I tell? as optional help, not a coverage answer. Allow correction/defer. Narrow options when an exact broad program is already known: TRICARE alone earns only its relevant subtype clarification if needed, not a repeat VA/CHAMPVA menu. Select any that apply preserves combinations such as VA health care plus another report without declaring all combinations legally valid. Known positives survive a partial unknown; retain G13 rather than erase them or force a single choice. Actual conflicting combinations need only a precise same-person/period clarification if consequential, under independently reviewed rules.
+
+**Brief reason when useful:** These programs have different Medicare rules, so I want to check the right one for you.
+
+**Prior-answer flow (synthetic, not customer facts):** T05 selects the broad VA, TRICARE or military coverage category. The person asks how starting Medicare would affect that coverage. Program identity changes the relevant rule investigation, so ask the original question within the same conversation. A clear answer such as TRICARE For Life supplies the reported program without another confirmation turn. Reuse known A/B status/dates; clarify only the additional actual facts the relevant supported rule needs. The original RC04/RC12 dependencies do not require a full A/B/creditable-history interview merely to name the program, and a program selection is not proof of enrollment or permission to change benefits.
+
+**Narrowed flow:** If T05 already says TRICARE but the subtype is consequentially unknown, ask Which TRICARE program do you have? with TRICARE For Life, Another TRICARE program and I'm not sure; typed program names/help remain. Other TRICARE is not necessarily sufficient when the actual rule needs a named subtype; ask its name only if that distinction changes supported requested work. Preserve current versus expected future program rather than rewriting a transition as already active.
+
+**Zero-ask flow:** T05/chat says I currently have TRICARE For Life, or I use VA health care and have Medicare. Reuse the named program(s), beneficiary/period and actual current-coverage scope. Ask no RC26 question or repeated programme confirmation unless a new consequential conflict/interpretation appears. If the task is simply What is Medicare? no military-program interview is needed. No demographic, pharmacy/provider name, A/B status, military service or age alone silently establishes a program/entitlement.
+
+**Help without a service-history interview:** Explain names in plain language and offer official program information if requested; accept an already available notice's typed program name. Do not demand membership numbers, rank, service dates, disability rating, proof uploads or account login simply to identify the reported coverage. Do not promise a particular card contains TRICARE For Life wording. If help does not identify the program, keep it unknown and show which personal finding remains unverified.
