+## RC16.C2 · Prior Medigap and relevant transition link · Approved shared-field child treatment
+
+**Necessity assessment first:** Keep only as a conditional missing-history/detail variant within approved RC16. This is the existing priorMedigap field, not another required step or a full policy-history interview. Ask only the exact prior-policy fact a supported requested Medigap protection/return check needs after T05/RC15/RC16/chat reuse. Prior Medigap is not needed automatically for first-eligibility-at-65 trial analysis, current Advantage, dissatisfaction or a general wish to explore Original Medicare; another sufficiently established protection can remove the need. If external policy/source limits mean collection cannot advance useful supported work, explain/defer rather than gather more history.
+
+**Original inventory question:** Did you have Medigap before it?
+
+**Original options:** Yes · No.
+
+**Critical copy/metadata issue:** It is unclear, Medigap may need its plain Medicare supplement name, and Yes/No needs unknown/help/correction routes. The inherited researchQuestion Was this your first Medicare Advantage plan? describes another field and must not substitute for prior-policy history. More importantly, ever owning Medigap is not the same as leaving it to join the relevant Advantage coverage. A scoped No to that transition does not mean never had Medigap. Preserve each question's actual meaning; do not coerce different answers into one unqualified historical boolean. The original inventory remains retained as traceability input; no source/runtime edit is claimed.
+
+**Proposed contextual question when a requested return-protection check needs the transition link:** Did you leave a Medicare supplement (Medigap) policy to join [relevant Medicare Advantage plan]?
+
+**Proposed unselected dropdown:** Yes · No · I'm not sure. Accept typed explanation, corrections and I'll answer later. Optional How can I tell? help explains the supplement distinction without requiring insurance expertise; uncertainty about whether a past policy was actually Medigap stays explicit. Use the actual beneficiary and known former policy/Advantage episode. If a rule needs only a narrower prior-ownership detail or another meaning, ask that fact instead; this wording is not a default lifetime-history question.
+
+**Brief reason when useful:** This helps check whether a protection applies when you return to a Medicare supplement.
+
+**Prior-answer flow (synthetic, not customer facts):** T05/chat identifies current Advantage and the user says I used to have [identified Medigap policy]; can I get that policy back? First-Advantage status/start are already known where needed. Prior ownership and the goal are known, but the supported requested return-right check still needs whether the person left that policy to join this episode. Ask only Did you leave your [former Medigap policy] to join [Advantage plan]? Do not ask Did you ever have Medigap? again. A clear Yes supplies the reported transition, not a verified protection or guarantee that the old policy remains available.
+
+**Scoped-negative example:** The person says I had Medigap years ago, but I did not leave it to join this Advantage plan. Preserve prior ownership plus the negative transition link. Do not overwrite history with never had Medigap or conclude no possible purchase route. If the existing priorMedigap scalar cannot retain these distinct meanings, keep raw reports and G04/G14 representation gaps; the dependent conclusion stays held rather than defaulting.
+
+**Zero-ask flow:** Earlier RC16/chat says I left my Medicare supplement to join my first Advantage plan. Reuse ownership and the explicitly stated transition link, with person/episode/period/provenance, and skip RC16.C2. A clear no-prior-policy report can likewise supply its actual scope. An unchanged unknown/defer is not retried through the child alias. If another sufficient protection resolves the requested check without this history, skip it. Closely related missing RC16 details can be collected naturally together only when needed; no default parent-plus-two-child sequence.
+
+**Former-policy details only when consequential:** If a specific return-to-that-policy finding needs it, reuse/ask the minimal missing former carrier/policy/period identity. Do not request member numbers, full documents or medical history merely to identify the reported policy. The user does not have to determine whether the insurer still offers it; availability/rights are separately checked from exact official/carrier evidence. Prior ownership, reason/date of ending, dropped-to-join link and actual former-policy availability are distinct. G04 now explicitly links current/former policy/return bindings to RC16/RC16.C2; no new active fields are silently added.
