+# Readiness source notes
+
+Retrieved October 22, 2026. Primary sources only. These are concise research notes, not licensed interpretation or accepted production rule packs. URLs may change; implementation must capture effective edition/year, source digest and named review receipt. `null` receipt/digest never means approved.
+
+## Federal vs Florida and current vs future year
+
+The active application has a 2027 Collier sample subset, sourced September 22, 2026, and a pending consumer acceptance registry. The calendar date here is October 2026. A 2026 cost table, the 2026 Florida statute edition and a 2027 plan record are different evidence scopes. No 2026 dollar threshold or income limit is copied into a 2027 estimate. Future-year legal changes and source applicability must be checked before a rule pack is approved. The readiness engine is not the data-acceptance engine.
+
+## S01 · Joining a plan
+
+[Joining a plan](https://www.medicare.gov/basics/get-started-with-medicare/get-more-coverage/joining-a-plan) · **Section:** Am I eligible?; Initial Enrollment Period; Other enrollment periods · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+MA requires A+B; standalone drug plans require A or B. Service area and enrollment periods matter. These are distinct from an application or verified eligibility.
+
+## S02 · Plan for Medicare
+
+[Plan for Medicare](https://www.ssa.gov/medicare) · **Section:** Plan for Medicare; When to sign up · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Age-based and non-age Medicare eligibility exist. An age or a coverage preference alone is not an enrollment determination.
+
+## S03 · When coverage starts
+
+[When coverage starts](https://www.medicare.gov/basics/get-started-with-medicare/sign-up/when-does-medicare-coverage-start) · **Section:** Initial Enrollment Period; Signing up for premium-free Part A later; Special Enrollment Period · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Initial enrollment and start dates depend on circumstances. First-day birthdays and retroactive Part A are material. Do not treat requested coverage month as an effective date.
+
+## S04 · Working past 65
+
+[Working past 65](https://www.medicare.gov/basics/get-started-with-medicare/medicare-basics/working-past-65) · **Section:** Health insurance from a job; COBRA; Before you sign up · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Current-employment group coverage can differ from retiree/individual coverage. Job and coverage end dates can differ. Employer confirmation matters; HSA contributions can be affected by Medicare start dates.
+
+## S05 · Who pays first?
+
+[Who pays first?](https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/coordination/who-pays-first) · **Section:** Current/former group coverage; employer-size paths; Federal Program/TRICARE paths · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+The age-65 coordination questions use 20 employees; the under-65 disability path uses 100. Multi-employer and ESRD circumstances need their own analysis. Do not apply one threshold to everyone.
+
+## S06 · COBRA coverage
+
+[COBRA coverage](https://www.medicare.gov/basics/get-started-with-medicare/medicare-basics/working-past-65/cobra-coverage) · **Section:** How does COBRA work with Medicare? · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+COBRA is continuation coverage and does not restart the Part B employment-based sign-up period. Possible gaps and payer coordination need review.
+
+## S07 · Retiree insurance
+
+[Retiree insurance](https://www.medicare.gov/basics/get-started-with-medicare/medicare-basics/working-past-65/retiree-insurance) · **Section:** Drug coverage; check before making decisions · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Joining outside coverage can affect retiree/family benefits; obtain benefits-administrator confirmation. Do not infer creditable drug status merely from the word retiree.
+
+## S08 · Creditable drug coverage
+
+[Creditable drug coverage](https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/part-d/basics/creditable-coverage) · **Section:** Why do I need creditable coverage?; What you should do · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+A creditable-coverage notice is relevant evidence. A gap of 63 days or more may create a Part D penalty; this is not the same clock as a Part B enrollment period.
+
+## S09 · When can I buy Medigap?
+
+[When can I buy Medigap?](https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/medigap/ready-to-buy/when) · **Section:** Federal-rights notice; Advantage trial/history questions; situation-specific answers · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Trial/guaranteed-issue possibilities depend on the exact event and history. First Medicare Advantage use and prior Medigap matter. Do not generalize one event-specific 63-day result to all cases.
+
+## S10 · Medigap basics
+
+[Medigap basics](https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/medigap/basics) · **Section:** Get Medigap Basics; Open Enrollment · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Federal Medigap open enrollment and later purchase are different. State rights may add protection. Medigap belongs with Original Medicare, not as a new Advantage supplement.
+
+## S11 · Change Medigap policy
+
+[Change Medigap policy](https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/medigap/ready-to-buy/change-policies) · **Section:** Can I change my Medigap policy? · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Outside protected situations switching can be limited. Do not cancel existing coverage on a provisional match; replacement/free-look details need review.
+
+## S12 · Florida Statutes 627.6741
+
+[Florida Statutes 627.6741](https://www.leg.state.fl.us/Statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&Search_String=&URL=0600-0699/0627/Sections/0627.6741.html) · **Section:** 2026 edition, subsection (1)(a)1 and (1)(a)2; (1)(b) · **Jurisdiction:** Florida · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Florida provides described six-month opportunities for qualifying residents including certain under-65 disability/ESRD beneficiaries, and a two-month opportunity after qualifying group-policy termination. Application to a particular event and future year requires expert review.
+
+## S13 · Florida Medicare Supplement oversight
+
+[Florida Medicare Supplement oversight](https://www.floir.gov/life-health/medicare-supplement) · **Section:** Overview; CHOICES rate search; FAQs · **Jurisdiction:** Florida · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+OIR is the state oversight/source route. A sample-rate search is not a binding personal quote or evidence that a particular policy is available to a person.
+
+## S14 · Help with drug costs
+
+[Help with drug costs](https://www.medicare.gov/basics/costs/help/drug-costs) · **Section:** Who gets Extra Help automatically?; applying; wrong amount · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Assistance affects drug costs. Certain Medicaid/MSP/SSI situations can lead to automatic Extra Help, but notice/current status still matters. Do not request bank records here.
+
+## S15 · Medicare Savings Programs
+
+[Medicare Savings Programs](https://www.medicare.gov/basics/costs/help/medicare-savings-programs) · **Section:** How to qualify; Qualified Medicare Beneficiary · **Jurisdiction:** federal/state · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+States determine MSP eligibility; annual thresholds and state treatment differ. Unknown assistance is not ineligibility; QMB-related cost-sharing protections need correct handling.
+
+## S16 · Special Needs Plans
+
+[Special Needs Plans](https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/health-plans/your-health-plan-options/SNP) · **Section:** Who can join an SNP?; eligibility requirements · **Jurisdiction:** federal/state/plan · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+SNPs have A/B, service-area and category-specific criteria. Being ill, having Extra Help, or wanting extra benefits does not by itself establish SNP eligibility.
+
+## S17 · Special Enrollment Periods
+
+[Special Enrollment Periods](https://www.medicare.gov/basics/get-started-with-medicare/get-more-coverage/joining-a-plan/special-enrollment-periods) · **Section:** Change where you live; lose coverage; Medicaid/Extra Help; special situations · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+An event can change enrollment opportunities. Allowed changes and dates are event-specific; Medicaid/Extra Help rules must not be reduced to an old quarterly rule.
+
+## S18 · Travel outside the U.S.
+
+[Travel outside the U.S.](https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/travel-outside-the-u.s.) · **Section:** Description; Coverage details · **Jurisdiction:** federal/plan · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Routine overseas care, rare Original Medicare exceptions and optional emergency benefits are different. A travel preference does not establish coverage.
+
+## S19 · Advantage provider networks
+
+[Advantage provider networks](https://www.medicare.gov/publications/11941-Understanding-Your-Medicare-Advantage-Plan.pdf) · **Section:** pp. 1–3, provider directories and checking with providers/plan · **Jurisdiction:** federal/plan · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Plan/provider confirmation and exact location matter. A directory identity or Medicare participation is not proof of participation in a particular Advantage contract.
+
+## S20 · RxNorm overview
+
+[RxNorm overview](https://www.nlm.nih.gov/research/umls/rxnorm/overview.html) · **Section:** Normalized names: ingredient, strength and dose form · **Jurisdiction:** technical/federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Drug identity includes strength and dose form. A normalized identifier alone does not establish a plan formulary match, clinical substitutability or coverage.
+
+## S21 · How drug plans work
+
+[How drug plans work](https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/part-d/what-drug-plans-cover/how-drug-plans-work) · **Section:** Formularies; pharmacy network · **Jurisdiction:** federal/plan · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Specific formulary and pharmacy information is required for coverage/cost checks. General drug coverage is not a promise about a named prescription.
+
+## S22 · Drug plan rules
+
+[Drug plan rules](https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/part-d/what-drug-plans-cover/plan-rules) · **Section:** Prior authorization; step therapy; quantity limits · **Jurisdiction:** federal/plan · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Coverage may carry restrictions or require an exception supported by the prescriber. Do not assume approval or transfer an old plan authorization to a new plan.
+
+## S23 · Outpatient prescription drugs
+
+[Outpatient prescription drugs](https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/prescription-drugs-outpatient) · **Section:** Description; Coverage details · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Some outpatient drugs can be paid under Part B under particular conditions. A Part-D-only estimator must not silently label such treatment uncovered.
+
+## S24 · Medicare costs
+
+[Medicare costs](https://www.medicare.gov/basics/costs/medicare-costs) · **Section:** Costs for Parts A/B/C/D and Medigap; year-specific tables · **Jurisdiction:** federal/plan · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Plan premium is not total spending. Premiums, care use, deductibles, drug costs and possible income adjustments must be labeled by year and inclusion basis.
+
+## S25 · VA and other insurance
+
+[VA and other insurance](https://www.va.gov/resources/va-health-care-and-other-insurance/) · **Section:** VA with Medicare; using each benefit · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+VA and Medicare are distinct care arrangements. VA drug coverage is relevant to Part D coordination; VA coverage is not a blanket reason to delay Part B.
+
+## S26 · Caregiver permission
+
+[Caregiver permission](https://www.medicare.gov/basics/get-started-with-medicare/using-medicare/5-tips-for-using-medicare) · **Section:** Tip 2: permission to talk to someone trusted · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Permission to research together is not authorization to retrieve Medicare account information or submit an application. Keep formal authorization outside an ordinary guest research chat.
+
+## S27 · Florida SHINE
+
+[Florida SHINE](https://www.floridashine.org/) · **Section:** Who We Are · **Jurisdiction:** Florida · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+Official free, unbiased, confidential counseling option. A referral is optional and does not imply an operating Daylight advisor transfer or insurer endorsement.
+
+## S28 · ESRD
+
+[ESRD](https://www.medicare.gov/basics/end-stage-renal-disease) · **Section:** Group coverage and coordination period · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+ESRD changes some coordination facts, including a possible 30-month period. Do not run ordinary age/disability employer-size logic on this case without specialist review.
+
+## S29 · Applying for Extra Help
+
+[Applying for Extra Help](https://www.ssa.gov/medicare/part-d-extra-help) · **Section:** Apply online; documents · **Jurisdiction:** federal · **Retrieved:** 2026-10-22.
+
+A formal assistance application requires financial information at SSA. This readiness check only records optional program status/interest and sends no application.
+
+## Interpretations explicitly not settled
+
+- Florida §627.6741(1)(a)2 uses a qualifying group-policy termination opportunity measured in months. Federal Medigap situation-specific examples may use days and different plan/history restrictions. Do not pick the longer window, merge them, or calculate a personal last day without a Florida Medicare subject-matter reviewer determining the actual event and applicable law.
+- The federal “When can I buy Medigap?” page is an interactive decision tree. A result for one set of answers must not be reused for another. Trial paths, prior policy availability and precise application periods remain expert-review gates. No blanket guaranteed-issue or universal underwriting conclusion.
+- Current-employment thresholds and any multi-employer/ESRD payer order require actual employer/program facts. An employee count alone is not sufficient.
+- State Medicaid status, QMB/MSP status, Extra Help and SNP alignment are related but distinct. Current monthly/special enrollment rules must be versioned; no legacy quarterly shortcut.
+- Drug normalization and provider identification are technical identities, not coverage. Old authorization/exception decisions do not automatically transfer to a new plan.
+- No pricing, provider access, eligibility or coverage promise follows merely from completing this check. Official application authorization and final plan confirmation remain separate.
+
+## Required review before implementation/release
+
+A qualified Medicare domain reviewer must approve trigger applicability, exact questions and resolution criteria; a Florida-qualified reviewer must resolve state Medigap rights; data owners must approve year/scope/versioned provider, formulary, pharmacy, benefits and rate releases; privacy/security owners must approve schema/sensitive-field changes. Record reviewer, role, date, review deadline and immutable rule/code/source fingerprints. Parent consumer acceptance remains fail-closed.
