+# Shortest sufficient conversation · consolidated design draft
+
+October 25–27, 2026 · D79, D52/D64/D73. **Design for review, not runtime changes or accepted Medicare policy.** The owner reaffirmed both tasks together: complete the critical information map and remove unnecessary asks. Individual prompt approval must not become approval of a long interview. Existing project inputs are reused; no new questionnaire or customer database is created.
+
+The **41 IDs remain a traceability inventory**: 10 baseline, 28 conditional parents, three documented children. A person's conversation is a capability-specific subset, with several fields often supplied by one reply. There is no fixed minimum or universal ten-question opening. The protected current UIs retain their contracts until a separately authorized implementation. T00 remains a brief welcome, not another required answer.
+
+The [full field map](CRITICAL_INFORMATION_FIELD_MAP.md) and [JSON](CRITICAL_INFORMATION_FIELD_MAP.json) record all seven dimensions for **78 existing paths**, plus separately identified semantic/representation gaps. The [owner review record](CRITICAL_INFORMATION_MAP_REVIEW.md) preserves prior approvals. Full table coverage is not professional approval or proof that all personal conclusions are supported.
+
+## Consolidated flow after the 41-entry review
+
+**Owner decision, October 27:** RC16.C2 stays within RC16 and asks only for missing details. All 41 inventory entries have now completed individual product review in their recorded scopes. The flow below assembles those decisions; examples of contextual wording are not a new questionnaire or approval of previously proposed exact copy. T00 inclusion is directed; its exact wording/placement remains proposed. T10's routine menu is removed; exact targeted copy remains contextual/proposed.
+
+**The routing rule:** Start from what the person wants to accomplish. Reuse what they already said, ask the next missing fact that changes that result, then reassess. A personal comparison needs consequential care and transition facts; a learning question or public fact lookup does not inherit that intake. There is no fixed required opening battery or mandatory sequence through these groups.
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    A[Brief welcome and reuse the stated goal] --> B{What is needed now?}
+    B -->|Learning| C[Answer the question with optional help]
+    B -->|Public lookup| D[Only missing reference location and year]
+    B -->|Personal check or comparison| E[Identify person and reuse relevant context]
+    E --> F{Consequential personal fact missing?}
+    F -->|Yes, and it can advance this check| G[Ask a specific missing detail or natural group]
+    G --> H{Reply}
+    H -->|Supplied or corrected| E
+    H -->|Unknown or deferred| I[Hold the dependent conclusion; continue useful work]
+    F -->|No| J[Check independent sources and applicable rules]
+    F -->|Collection cannot advance the held check| I
+    D --> J
+    J -->|Sufficient for the claim| K[Return the supported scoped result]
+    J -->|Evidence or release held| I
+```
+
+Corrections and scope changes can occur anywhere. An unchanged unknown is not automatically re-asked through another ID. A new goal can open a new branch. A blocked/deferred stop is recorded separately from completing the original requested conclusion.
+
+### Opening and shared context
+
+**T00, proposed welcome:**
+
+> Hi, I'm Daylight, your AI Medicare guide. I can help you understand Medicare, explore coverage choices and figure out what to check next.
+>
+> We'll take it at your pace. You can ask questions, change an answer or say “I don't know.”
+
+No separate required Start answer. If the request already names a task, begin helping. Otherwise T01 asks **What would you like help with today?** with the four approved options: **Understand Medicare · Find coverage · Review existing coverage · Something else**. T02 familiarity remains optional when useful; choosing a goal does not establish familiarity.
+
+| Conversation group and existing links | What the person sees when needed | What is reused or skipped |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Recipient · RC01 | A short clarification of whose situation is being discussed, only if unclear. | Explicit self/helper context; no beneficiary interview for general learning. Never merge helper and beneficiary facts. |
+| Relevant location · T03 + RC02 | **What ZIP code do you live in?** Ask only a still-missing county/home detail if required. | Already supplied beneficiary home; uniquely sourced county relationship with provenance. Public browsing can use an explicit reference location without claiming residency. |
+| Intended period · T04 + RC03 | **When do you need Medicare coverage to start?** Choose start month / Already on Medicare / Not sure. For existing coverage, clarify only the relevant review period. | An explicit month and year or review year; desired start never substitutes for actual enrollment dates. |
+| Current coverage · T05, RC04, RC07, RC09, RC26; intention RC17 | **What health coverage do you have now?** Accept free text or the reviewed multiple coverage choices, with uncertainty/help. | Extract the explicit A/B, Original/Advantage, job-linked insurance, program and intention facts from one reply. Ask only what remains needed; current, pending and former coverage stay distinct. |
+| Doctors · T06 + RC21 | **Which doctors or hospitals would you like to keep?** Free text, followed by a compact echo of actual available identity/office matches for confirmation. | Existing names/offices and confirmed matches. Resolve only ambiguous items. None to check, unknown and defer have different meanings. Identity does not establish network participation. |
+| Medicines · T07 + RC22 | **What prescriptions do you take?** Free text. Resolve only a consequential missing product detail, with sourced selections when available. | Explicit product/strength/form; echo consequential interpretations. No automatic fill, pharmacy or administration interview. None, unknown and defer stay distinct. |
+| Away care · T08 + RC20 | **Will you need routine care away from home?** Local only / Elsewhere in the U.S. / Outside the U.S. / Not sure. | Known relevant care need/destination, including same-state away care. Ask only missing place/care meaning, and duration only if a source condition requires it. |
+| Preferences · T09, T10; optional RC25 | **How would you prefer to balance monthly payments and costs when you get care?** Lower monthly payments / More predictable costs / No preference yet. | Explicit preference already given. Clarify a must-have or numerical limit only if useful to the requested comparison; no routine closing menu or budget request. |
+
+These are reusable groups, not eight required turns. Ask only the subset needed for the task, in an order that follows the person's reply. Before an unqualified personal fit comparison, unresolved relevant doctors/medicines/away-care or transition scope cannot silently mean no needs. General path teaching and partial factual comparisons can continue with clearly stated limits.
+
+### What unlocks additional details
+
+Each row describes a dependency, not an automatic follow-up to the previous row. Exact examples name the known policy/person/medicine and omit facts already supplied.
+
+| Branch | Actual unlock and targeted follow-up | Suppressed asks and limits |
+| --- | --- | --- |
