+
+The 11 runtime wording variants and 31 detail controls remain overlapping implementation forms. They are not 42 additional information requirements. RC29 is an external-source guard, RC30 a held future application review; neither is another intake prompt.
+
+## Capability-specific shortest paths and blockers
+
+These are proposed demand rules for design review, not an approved executable insurance policy. The full field map specifies each leaf. Unknown never satisfies a consequential required fact, but a missing preference does not block otherwise supported work.
+
+| Requested work | Smallest relevant input family, including conditional expansion | Missing facts block which conclusion | Independent external gate |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Explain a Medicare concept or general path tradeoffs | The actual question; optional T02 only if useful. | Only an ambiguity preventing an accurate answer; no personal profile gate. | Accepted general source scope; no implied personal fit. |
+| Browse published local/year facts | Required home/reference geography and explicit year from T03/RC02, T04/RC03 or a known fact. No T05–T10 by default. | Exact local/year claim if required scope is unresolved. Unique ZIP derivation stays sourced, not verified residence. | Exact service area/year and source acceptance; sample browsing remains explicitly labeled. Current ZIP/county gate compatibility must be reviewed before any narrower geographic rule is implemented. |
+| Prepare a personal path comparison | Clear task/person, relevant current coverage/parts, scope/year, consequential intended timing, explicit doctor/medicine/away-care scope; expand only material transition/rights details. | An unqualified personal fit/path conclusion that depends on unresolved facts. Specific Medigap issueability/transition conclusions need their own branch. | Market scope, rules, exact benefits, independence/comparison acceptance; never supplied by intake completion. |
+| Check a named provider | Relevant person/task/year/path/plan, T06 name(s) and confirmed RC21 identity/office; T08/RC20 only for consequential care geography. | That provider/office result and an all-requested-providers claim. Other independently supported results remain visible. | Trusted identity source plus path-appropriate access/network evidence. Identity confirmation is not coverage. |
+| Check a named medicine's coverage | Relevant exact plan/year and T07/RC22 name/strength/form; RC24 only if the requested coverage issue needs it. | That product's exact coverage/restriction result and an all-medicines claim. Missing fill/pharmacy facts do not automatically block a pharmacy-independent coverage check. | Trusted product identity, exact formulary/restrictions and reviewed applicable policy. |
+| Estimate a specific fill's cost | Drug identity plus RC23 quantity/units, days supply, exact pharmacy/location and channel; relevant assistance only for adjusted costs. | Exact affected fill/annual estimate when its required scenario input is missing. | Pharmacy identity/network and accepted exact pricing/model/source evidence. No default fill scenario. |
+| Personal enrollment/transition timing | Requested period, relevant actual parts/date/basis and only consequential event/work/end-date/notice/HSA/program facts (RC04–RC14/RC26/RC27). | The particular deadline, start, payer-order, deferral or contribution consequence depending on the missing fact. Precise anchors/Part A/HSA gaps are not closed by ageBand/B date/yes-no. | Official enrollment/notice evidence and qualified reviewed timing/coordination policy. |
+| Personal Medigap rights/replacement | Relevant state/basis/age/B start, actual event/notice and only material Advantage/prior-Medigap/replacement history (RC15–RC17). | A specific buying-right, issueability or safe-replacement conclusion. | Reviewed federal/state policy, official history and actual issueability evidence where required. |
+| SNP qualification | Relevant exact type, ordinary scope/parts and minimal specific RC19 program/qualification report; RC18 only where pertinent. | That type's eligibility/fit claim. Unverified is not ineligible or an automatically omitted option. | Actual program/plan qualification and accepted policy. |
+| Personal total cost or budget fit | Exact requested scenario, period/components, relevant coverage/fills/use and any material assistance; optional RC25 amount/basis only if actually applied. | Comprehensive personal total/savings/affordability or budget-fit claims missing components/meaning. | Accepted components, applicability, model and evidence; published premiums/IRMAA tables alone cannot close this. |
+| Priority-specific explanation | Explicit relevant preference/constraint from prior reports; T09/T10 only for a real remaining ambiguity. | Only a claim that an unclear or unverified stated priority is honored. | Any factual claim of satisfaction requires its independent evidence; no numerical weights or economic steering. |
+
+RC02/RC03 and internal item references are data requirements, not automatic consumer questions. A control field can be derived from an explicit report under a declared mapping, without asking the person to confirm the same substance twice. A “details supplied” flag cannot replace the actual details.
+
+### Optional self-discovery help · owner direction, October 26
+
+When a consequential question uses unfamiliar terms, offer concise optional conceptual help (for example What's the difference) and practical answer-finding help (How can I tell / Where can I find this). RC07 is the reviewed example; adapt the wording and evidence to the actual field rather than adding universal help questions. Keep explanations local to the current question, preserve known answers and return to the same unresolved selection/free text with I'm still not sure available. No mandatory lesson/quiz, new primary question ID or automatic capability readiness follows from reading help.
+
+Help interactions count as user/assistant turns and elapsed reading/response time; count any actual additional Daylight information requests normally. No-question explanatory content introduces no extra required profile fact, but its burden cannot be hidden by screen counts. RC07's official comparison/card/account links are general education and user-directed ways to inspect coverage, not Daylight account access, verified enrollment or permission to collect identifiers. Keep exact copy and evidence scope in the owner review.
+
+## Natural groups, not mandatory stages
+
+- **Welcome/task:** T00 with T01 when needed. If the person opens with a clear question, answer it and reuse that intent.
+- **Relevant scope:** recipient before personal facts; location/year together when the requested source needs them. Ask only missing pieces.
+- **Current situation:** a natural current-coverage/intended-change reply can supply T05, T04 and explicit RC04/RC07/RC09/RC26 facts. Do not infer the unprovided ones.
+- **Provider identity:** T06 free text → one compact candidate echo → confirm clear matches together, resolve only ambiguous items. Reuse office details for RC21.
+- **Medicine identity:** T07 free text → confirm consequential name/strength/form interpretations. A supported requested price task opens only still-missing RC23 fill/pharmacy facts. A specifically requested quantity-limit/pharmacy-network finding reuses only its pertinent facts; no full pricing interview follows, and capability metadata remains a review gap.
+- **Consequential exceptions:** relevant employment, Medigap history, assistance, events or unusual cases open only their missing branch, with a brief reason.
+- **Tradeoff clarification:** no routine T10 closing menu. A targeted clarification is optional and only useful when an actual unresolved priority affects the requested output.
+
+Grouped wording is assembled from the existing IDs, not a newly numbered questionnaire. Count the constituent information requests even when a single message collects several facts.
+
+## Questions, turns and time
+
+Three measures are mandatory; none is a proxy for the others.
+
+1. **Questions asked:** count displayed information-request prompts, including confirmations and repeats. Also count **atomic information requests** within them: one prompt asking employment end and health-coverage end is one prompt and two detail requests. Internal IDs, derived dispositions and source lookups are not customer questions. Per-doctor confirmations remain distinct requests even when grouped.
+2. **Conversation turns:** count every submitted user response and every assistant message, including help, confirmations, correction and recovery. One multi-fact reply is one user turn; clicking several inputs before submitting is not several replies. Keep system processing separate. Screens/clicks alone do not measure the conversation.
+3. **Elapsed time:** wall-clock from task entry/T00 to the useful scoped outcome or explicit blocked/deferred stop. Distinguish active interaction, user pauses, system/external waiting and the reported-input milestone. Do not relabel a blocked recommendation as completion of the original task. Define inactivity segmentation before human measurement; no elapsed times are invented here.
+
+Evaluate equivalent requested outcomes and comparable case complexity. Report unfinished/unknown cases, correction rates, repeated asks, source holds and staff work alongside completed cases. A shorter message count that increases reading/recall/correction burden is not an established improvement.
+
+The [synthetic trace audit](CONVERSATION_TRACE_AUDIT.md) counts declared prompts, atomic requests and turns for representative design examples. It is not a running app, consumer test, validated policy evaluation or measured human completion time. Every human elapsed-time observation remains **not measured**. Its purpose is to catch duplicate asks, unknown loops, internal-control questions and pricing-only data collected for coverage-only tasks before implementation.
+
+Future instrumentation should aggregate counts/reasons and minimized references under the existing privacy rules; this design does not authorize raw transcripts, health-name telemetry, new retention, paid AI calls or outreach.
+
+## Limits and next review
+
+The field map's G01–G14 gaps explicitly cover precise eligibility anchors, Part A/contribution chronology, personal premium applicability, exact current policy, trusted entity bindings, multiple care locations/needs, total-cost scenarios, assistance detail, payer-order context, per-medicine setting, nuanced constraints, unlisted coverage and generic corrections. Each has a question/known-report link, all seven mapping parts and the conclusions withheld. They are not silently added fields or new universal questions.
+
+Keep separate the non-intake permissions for AI transfer, saving/sensitive notes, family sharing and any supported human/fulfillment action. RC01 helper status grants none of those. Source guard RC29 and held application boundary RC30 cannot be cleared by answers. No independent source acceptance, enrollment, recommendation release or implementation is claimed.
+
+Review **consolidation/path decisions** one at a time against this whole map. An individual prompt is reviewed only in its path, with its incremental missing facts, reuse and measured or unmeasured burden visible. All 41 individual product treatments have now been reviewed in their recorded scopes. This consolidated presentation, exact proposed copy, unresolved semantic/evidence gaps and any implementation retain their separate review status. The ten baseline items are not the completion denominator for either task.
