+# Progress against the fifteen company capabilities
+
+November 2, 2026. Assessment of the local Daylight workspace against the owner's company map. **Progress is substantial but uneven: the advisor experience and research foundation are much further along than accepted personal decisions, operating service and business proof.** The task now is to connect and validate those parts, with clear owners, rather than add another broad product specification.
+
+The [primary narrative](../company/README.md) describes the intended company. The table distinguishes current mechanics from that completed promise. “Working locally” means implemented behavior with inspected code or scoped technical evidence; it does not mean production, independent domain acceptance or demonstrated consumer benefit. “Partial foundation” means important pieces exist but the end-to-end task is incomplete. “Specified” means strategy/contracts dominate the available evidence. No overall percentage is justified across these unlike capabilities.
+
+## Capability ledger
+
+| Component | Current maturity | What exists | Principal gap and next deliverable |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **CAP-01 User experience and education** | Working locally; user benefit unproved | :8893 natural conversation, source footnotes, contextual teaching visuals, one composer, correction, editable preparation and responsive engineering evidence. The seventeen-concept visit record separates exposure from comprehension. | Observe first-time Collier users doing supported tasks; assess understanding, burden, correction and accessibility. Complete sustained current-version model evaluation. [Product review](../reviews/2026-11-02-project-readiness/PRODUCT_REVIEW.md). |
+| **CAP-02 Customer understanding and profile** | Working locally; incomplete detail coverage | Forty-one conditional meanings, scoped reported facts, provenance, unknown/deferred states, correction/invalidation and optional same-browser saving. Independently authored persona expectations provide meaningful checks. | Resolve thirteen held/unwritten added detail paths and two legacy fields without writers; prove consequential input confirmation at the end of information gathering. Guest saving is not accounts, cross-device or family sharing. [Profile evidence](../../audit-evidence/advisor-persona-coverage-20261102/README.md). |
+| **CAP-03 Data ingestion and maintenance** | Substantial acquisition; maintenance partial | Source collectors, retained versions, all fifteen selected layer imports, source STOP persistence, resumable jobs and checksums. | Turn source-specific scripts into permitted recurring connectors and a candidate-change → review → release → rollback cycle. Demonstrate one real permitted update before claiming dependable maintenance. [Infrastructure](../../infrastructure/daylight-data/README.md). |
+| **CAP-04 Consolidation and normalization** | Substantial transport; domain meaning partial | Exact IDs, source periods, original payloads, qualifications, amounts and lineage survive into roughly 17.8 million projections. | Complete typed benefit/condition, drug/unit, provider/site/network, policy-event and Medigap models. Initial JSON/projection import is not complete normalization. [Data review](../reviews/2026-11-02-project-readiness/DATA_REVIEW.md). |
+| **CAP-05 Data review and evidence governance** | Strong foundation; review throughput incomplete | Sealed revisions, exact hashes, holds, named gaps, source/interpretation distinctions and narrow accepted references. | Finish source-first whole-offering reconciliation and independent review; implement practical review ownership/queue and executable exact authority loading. Preserve the full r9 denominator and accepted r4 reference. [Current L03](../data/l03-ma-benefits-2026-11-02-whole-offering-r12/README.md). |
+| **CAP-06 Data integration and verification** | Internal research integrated; personal verification held | Seventy-two MA identities, benefit and quality research views, explicit medicine/provider-site candidates and a connected internal advisor journey. | Establish exact plan/year/product/site/period/condition relationships and current supported outcomes. A selected drug or clinician candidate does not establish coverage, equivalence or participation. [Connected milestone](../../audit-evidence/comparison-milestone-20261102/README.md). |
+| **CAP-07 Coverage analysis and plan recommendation** | Preparation and contracts; consumer decisions held | Coverage-path-first design, separate report/evidence gates, comparison adapter and synthetic method helpers. Current real response evaluates zero consumer plans and permits no personal ordering/recommendation. | Accepted market scope, current-coverage baseline, cost/access/rule checks, reviewed decision method, authority replay, end confirmation and independently reviewed outputs. [Comparison contract](../product/plan-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md). |
+| **CAP-08 Agentic conversation and execution loop** | Working local conversation; research/action loop partial | Interpret → validate reports → compose answer/teaching/next question; correction, bounded visit memory, failure recovery and preparation. Internal identity tools are connected separately. | Allow the advisor to execute accepted personal research and explain tool findings through controlled purposes. Research rows currently remain outside consumer findings and model context. Prove task completion and escalation beyond conversation. [Ongoing advisor](../product/ONGOING_ADVISOR_FLOW_2026-11-01.md). |
+| **CAP-09 Trade-off discussion and decision support** | Educational discussion; personal scenario support partial | Coverage-route teaching, captured priorities and pure comparison/scenario helpers. | Explicit constraints, understandable priority sensitivity, accepted costs/access evidence and connected what-if correction/replay. Current response has no inferred preference weights and does not evaluate hard constraints. [Decision rules](../product/plan-comparison-2026-11-01/DECISION_RULES.md). |
+| **CAP-10 Trust and independence** | Binding principles and technical safeguards; full proof open | Commercial exclusion requirements, source scope, explicit holds, correction controls and tests rejecting commercial canaries/unreviewed fields. | Complete I01–I10 against the actual released decision flow; demonstrate reproducible reasons, market/exclusion transparency, revocation and challenge handling. Independent source coverage and independent economics are separate obligations. [Acceptance](../product/INDEPENDENCE_ACCEPTANCE.md). |
+| **CAP-11 Human service and fulfillment** | Preparation implemented; service operation unspecified in key places | Editable/copyable/printable follow-up checklists; dated local counseling references. Preparation explicitly sends nothing. | Named qualified operating route, exception owner, response targets, permissioned handoff and receipt/status tracking; approved enrollment integration before claiming transactions. No staffed service or completed enrollment demonstrated in this review. [Architecture guide](../planning/ARCHITECTURE_ALIGNMENT_AND_IMPLEMENTATION_2026-11-02.md). |
+| **CAP-12 Ongoing customer relationship** | Resume foundation; continuing service specified | Optional seven-day guest profile, sensitive-save separation, explicit deletion and current-visit continuity. | Purposeful durable identity/permission design, changed-drug/provider review, authorized follow-up, family access and cross-device recovery. RAM learning is not a persistent relationship. [Strategy stages](../product/STRATEGIC_THESIS.md#roadmap-proof-before-expansion). |
+| **CAP-13 Engineering, privacy and reliability** | Significant local infrastructure; team/cloud readiness incomplete | Packaged PostgreSQL service, pinned dependencies, migrations/roles, bounded internal queries, local permissions and an integrity-checked backup. | Curated reproducible Git checkout, CI, cloud target binding, clean restore plus off-machine recovery, secret/role operations, incident ownership and deliberate multiworker state/budget behavior. [Engineering review](../reviews/2026-11-02-project-readiness/ENGINEERING_REVIEW.md). |
+| **CAP-14 Distribution, partnerships and economics** | Strategy and measurement definitions | First-transition independent-research audience, partner hypotheses, free consumer proposition and neutrality requirement. | Choose one acquisition route; measure recruitment, completed tasks, acquisition/support/data-review/AI costs and contribution across keep/defer/uncompensated outcomes. No repeatable acquisition or measured unit economics found in reviewed sources. [Thesis](../product/STRATEGIC_THESIS.md). |
+| **CAP-15 Quality measurement and organizational learning** | Strong technical checks; consumer/operating proof absent | Persona expectations, privacy/failure tests, independent technical probes and dated audit packets; cohort measure definitions. | One current-build evaluation record, held-out real-model tasks, qualified factual adjudication, observed comprehension/control and staff/outcome measurement. Historical test counts do not certify the merged build or prove customer value. [Measures](../product/STRATEGIC_THESIS.md#evidence-definitions-for-the-first-cohort). |
+
+## What is strong and what is slowing progress
+
+The project has invested in the difficult foundations: preserving conditions rather than flattening benefits, keeping unknown evidence visible, retaining corrections, isolating commercial incentives and restricting what can become a personal finding. The full local database and internal research bridge are real advances. The advisor is substantially more capable than the older README's “visual guide with help” description.
+
+The largest product gap is the distance between **describing circumstances conversationally** and **finishing accepted personal research with an understandable choice**. The existing engine intentionally keeps the six consumer purposes held: display, comparison, ranking, recommendation, quote and enrollment. Separately gated L01/r4 reference readers have their own exact acceptance; those receipts do not release the current research bridge or its projections. Unblocking the complete flow takes reviewed semantics, identity/temporal joins, decision methods and release machinery, not only another interface improvement.
+
+The largest organizational gap is reproducibility. A collaborator cannot recover the current advisor, evidence selection and permissions from the small committed repository alone. Current navigation mixes dates and variants, local paths are integral to some evidence bindings, and a decoding backup has not been restored on a clean machine. These are tractable engineering tasks and can progress while substantive source review continues.
+
+The largest business uncertainty is consumer and operating proof. There is no demonstrated cohort in the reviewed material showing that people understand more, make fewer consequential errors, finish useful work with manageable effort, or can be served sustainably. The company thesis is coherent; its benefit and economics need observation.
+
+## Data coverage is not one completion badge
+
+The [detailed L01–L15 review](../reviews/2026-11-02-project-readiness/DATA_REVIEW.md) records current selected populations and remaining conditions. Important distinctions:
+
+- L01 has an accepted **published federal reference**. That is not a personal entitlement or cost calculator.
+- L02 retains **72 observed MA offerings**, with market completeness and verified availability still unresolved; L04 retains **10 PDP identities**. The 72 are neither a verified full consumer market nor the whole coverage-path universe.
+- L03 acquired all **144 required main SB/EOC document slots**. Full semantic reconciliation is still open. The r12 pilot and any proposed atomic children cannot silently change r9's **392,570 obligations**.
+- L05–L08 support real drug/pharmacy/provider research, but criteria stops, units, exact network/site/period ties and individual access/cost findings remain material gaps.
+- L09 source/parity work is further along than its old README suggests. L10 Medigap has substantial filing evidence but an unknown all-market denominator, source-period conditions and no binding quote engine.
+- L11–L14 retain useful rule references; personal event/date/application interpretations and exact review remain distinct. L15's dated counseling contacts are neither appointment availability nor an operating Daylight handoff service.
+
+## How progress should be reported from here
+
+Use capability-specific deliverables with an owner, scope/year, exact code/data versions, observed result and remaining limit. Keep five states separate: implemented, technically checked, domain reviewed, accepted for a named use, and proven useful to users. A single “done” checkbox loses the distinctions most important to Daylight.
+
+Use the [Collier pilot backlog](COLLIER_MVP.md) to join the existing workstreams. The new company map is an index across that work, not fifteen new software services, fifteen mandatory intake stages, or permission to reduce the existing data program.
