+# The 2026 Collier controlled pilot
+
+Owner confirmed November 2, 2026: **2026 controlled pilot first**. The initial audience is first-time Medicare enrollees researching independently, with permissioned caregiver participation where relevant. The company promise remains useful education and completed research leading to an informed coverage choice at the person's pace.
+
+The current advisor can support a bounded education/preparation evaluation after study/privacy readiness is established. It cannot yet support a claim of an accepted personal-choice MVP. The milestones below distinguish that early learning opportunity from the complete coverage-choice service. They do not reduce the full L03 obligations or treat a narrow pilot as full L03 completion.
+
+## Three near-term milestones and one operating extension
+
+| Milestone | Supported outcome | Current state | Exit evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **A. Reproducible team research build** | Another contributor can check out code, run fictional tests and inspect authorized research through the same controls. | Local implementation exists; repository, archive closure, clean restore and portable target binding remain incomplete. | Reviewed Git tree, reproducible dependencies, preserved engine lock, minimal approved evidence/fixture bootstrap, isolated successful restore, role/STOP/held-purpose checks and one exact merged-build result. |
+| **B. Controlled education and preparation pilot** | A participant explains relevant coverage paths, corrects reports, understands uncertainty and leaves with useful supported next steps. | Substantial local product; no observed consumer cohort established by this review. | Named study owner, consent/handling rules, fixed task/year/capability scope, qualified teaching review, completion/correction/comprehension observations and a clear unsupported-case route. |
+| **C. Accepted Collier coverage-choice MVP** | The advisor completes supported personal checks, compares paths then policies, explains tradeoffs and helps the person make a supported choice or keep/defer. | Incomplete: real consumer comparison/recommendation purposes remain held. | Exact accepted market/data/method/output scope, person-input end confirmation, current medicine/provider/cost/rule checks as required, reproducible decision record, independent review, I01–I10 and observed consumer understanding/control. |
+| **D. Supported fulfillment and continuing service** | The person can complete an explicitly supported transaction or permissioned handoff, then receive the promised continuing help. | Preparation only; operating route and continuing service not demonstrated. | Named qualified operator/platform, specific transfer/action permission, application/handoff status receipts and exception recovery; separate authorized follow-up/retention proof. |
+
+Milestone B can proceed in parallel with evidence work. It must be described as education and preparation, with no personal ranking, invented research results or claims that a sample is a recommendation. Milestone C is the substantive choice promise in the narrative. One reconciled plan is a vertical proof of the pipeline, not a fair full-market comparison.
+
+## Scope decisions already made
+
+- Geography: Collier County for the controlled pilot. National teaching remains distinct from county/year-specific plan facts.
+- Benefit year: 2026. Retained 2027 sample records stay visibly separate and cannot supply missing 2026 facts. Any later 2027 expansion needs its own exact identity, benefit, formulary, network, pricing and policy work.
+- Primary development surface: :8893 advisor-first; protect :8890, :8891, :8896 and their stores. This is not a declaration that :8893 is a public production service.
+- Intake: retain natural report capture and targeted ambiguity clarification. The latest owner direction requires one editable end summary and confirmation immediately before requested personal comparison/recommendation; not a new universal questionnaire or per-message acceptance cards.
+- Coverage scope: paths before policies, including Original Medicare with optional Medigap/separate Part D, MA and relevant other coverage. Current coverage, keep and defer remain legitimate outcomes.
+- Independence: commercial economics do not enter substantive decisions, AI context, selection or research priorities. A preferred fulfillment route cannot narrow the evidence universe.
+
+## Actionable backlog
+
+Priority describes dependency/impact, not a promised date. Accountable roles are proposed; the founder still needs to assign actual people. Existing authorizations and workstreams continue. These entries cross-reference the [sixteen-step architecture guide](../planning/ARCHITECTURE_ALIGNMENT_AND_IMPLEMENTATION_2026-11-02.md), rather than launch a duplicate program.
+
+| ID / priority | Deliverable and gap type | Accountable role | Dependencies | Acceptance evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **P01 / first** | Curate current code/docs for the confirmed public GitHub destination; exclude private state and bulk evidence. Internal engineering. | Engineering lead + publication reviewer | Publication policy, outgoing-history review | Explicit selected paths, content/license/secret review, clean clone and fixture tests; no missing pinned engine files. |
+| **P02 / first** | Restore research DB, roles/config and referenced evidence on an isolated target; establish encrypted off-machine recovery. Internal work plus actual hosting/account choice. | Infrastructure owner | Full backup/archive manifest, capacity and target compatibility | Successful SQL execution/restore, source/hash/key/row/qualification parity, held-purpose/STOP behavior, timed recovery and rollback receipt. Decode-only backup is insufficient. |
+| **P03 / first** | Confirm one current merged advisor build and capability ledger. Internal engineering. | Advisor lead + independent reviewer | Concurrent changes settled into explicit revisions | Relevant offline suites and responsive behavior against exact merged code; known doctor-entry incident either reproduced/resolved or explicitly monitored with permitted diagnostics. |
+| **P04 / first** | Complete H5652-002 whole-offering semantic pilot and exact review. Internal semantics plus named source blockers. | Benefit lead + independent Medicare reviewer | r9/r12 lineage; permitted missing source evidence | All 4,675 original obligations accounted by meaning/disposition; exact proposed-child before/after accounting; independent interpretation and explicit new-release decision. No inherited r4 acceptance. |
+| **P05 / next, parallel** | Complete remaining full L03 approved scope using the reviewed pilot method. Internal work and actual source dependencies. | Benefit/review owners by offering | P04 method, review capacity | Preserved r9 baseline of 392,570 obligations, with exact before/after accounting for any independently reviewed adopted revision; all original obligations and 153 historical hold groups retain explicit lineage/disposition. This remains an obligation even if B is released first. |
+| **P06 / next, parallel** | Establish accepted 2026 relevant-market and availability scope. Domain/source-use review. | Plan-data lead + domain reviewer | L02/L04 identities, restrictions, categories and geography | Explicit expected universe or exact disclosed limits; accepted availability/status/restrictions and supported consumer use. Seventy-two observed MA rows alone are insufficient. |
+| **P07 / next** | Implement one accepted consequential personal verification chain, then extend by capability. Internal integration plus exact source acceptance. | Data integration lead + domain reviewer | Current reports, exact drug/provider/site/outlet/plan/year identity | Accepted supported result with conditions/date/unknowns, correction invalidation, source STOP, expiry and replay. Candidate selection never masquerades as coverage. |
+| **P08 / next, parallel** | Close cost, Medigap and policy applicability methods needed by declared tasks. Domain modeling and review. | Cost/rule lead + qualified reviewers | L01/L05–L07/L10–L14 relevant evidence and current personal circumstances | Unit/dose/phase/subsidy/refill assumptions, access/rights/time qualifications and independently checked examples; estimates distinct from quotes. |
+| **P09 / critical to C** | Build actual evidence-purpose authority loading, freshness/revocation, original accepted-reference replay and immutable release selection. Internal engineering + exact acceptances. | Evidence platform/release owner | Reviewed source/method/output records | Held/stale/mismatched/revoked releases fail closed; approved exact use works; original r4/r1 receipts replay without blanket promotion. |
+| **P10 / critical to C** | Complete end-confirmed inputs, path-first comparison, constraints/scenarios, reasons and minimized decision journal. Internal product/decision work. | Decision lead + product/domain reviewer | P06–P09 for real outputs; synthetic cases can proceed now | Reconstruct decision from permitted inputs/evidence/method versions, compare keep/defer, revise priorities, challenge/correct and replay without commercial influence. |
+| **P11 / first for B** | Establish controlled pilot protocol and measure real understanding and effort. Consumer proof. | Research/product owner + qualified content reviewer | Stable B build, participant permission, supported task list | Participant/task denominators, failures and missing observations, severity rubric, comprehension/control/correction/completion and staff minutes. |
+| **P12 / first before public service** | Threat/role, privacy, retention, recovery and incident operations; explicit deployment topology. Internal operations + actual provider terms. | Security/operations owner | Target architecture, data-flow map, purpose/permissions | Access/deletion/incident/restore exercises; no new raw-chat persistence; isolated customer boundary; concurrency/budget and restart behavior tested. |
+| **P13 / before D** | Choose qualified human/fulfillment route and prove an exception/handoff drill. Operating decision/vendor dependency. | Founder + qualified operations lead | Recipient/platform, supported actions, consent/content rules | Accepted recipient/context, status and recovery receipts, actual staff owner/response target; neutral route for unsupported fulfillment. |
+| **P14 / parallel pilot learning** | Test one acquisition channel and economics across neutral outcomes. Business proof. | Founder/growth + operations analyst | P11 cohort permission and cost definitions | Measured acquisition, support/review/rework/AI/hosting costs; outcome mix and contribution with keep/defer/uncompensated outcomes retained. |
+| **P15 / later** | Permissioned continuing review service. Product/operations plus durable identity design. | Relationship/service owner | Accepted checks, refresh cycle, identity/retention/notification permissions | A real authorized change → review → useful follow-up → resolution cycle; retention and service effort, not just profile storage. |
+
+## Genuine external dependencies versus work that can continue
+
+The known optional-dental guide and amendment/source leads in the L03 pilot have specific timeouts/403 stops and missing exact bytes. L05 has named access-stopped or incomplete criteria populations. Source-use and independent domain approvals, a real cloud account/region/cost choice, and a qualified fulfillment platform/operator can require external decisions. Record the exact missing source or decision, owner, permitted route and closure evidence. Moving tools to a new machine must not bypass a source STOP.
+
+Substantial internal work remains even while those dependencies are open: extraction repair, semantic grain/condition reconciliation, review queue design, domain joins, purpose authority, decision scenarios, clean restore, portable configuration, tests and consumer research on already supported education/preparation. Do not describe all remaining work as external or blocked on hosting.
+
+## Pilot measurement and decision rules
+
+Before recruiting, agree the actual tasks, participant count, observation window, qualified reviewer and decision thresholds. This review does not invent a passing score or claim a cohort occurred. Use the [existing cohort definitions](../product/STRATEGIC_THESIS.md#evidence-definitions-for-the-first-cohort):
+
+| Measure | What to record |
+| --- | --- |
+| Factual correctness | Reviewed claims/tasks, material errors by severity, unsupported statements, appropriate abstention and corrections. |
+| Understanding | Participant explanation of coverage paths, meaningful tradeoffs and unresolved checks; confidence separately. |
+| Control | Successful fact/priority corrections, permission understanding, recovery without restart and incorrect confirmations. |
+| Useful completion | Requested supported tasks completed, failures, abandonment, time/effort and remaining steps. Enrollment alone is not success. |
+| Operational effort | Staff minutes, source review/maintenance time, repeated work and exception cause. |
+| Economics | Acquisition, AI, hosting, licensed support and maintenance costs across the neutral outcome mix. |
+| Continuing value | Later authorized use and resolved changed circumstances; distinguish actual follow-up from intent. |
+
+For interaction research, compare the excellent adaptive form, directed conversation and hybrid using the same evidence and confirmation standards. Test the value of evidence depth separately with interface held fixed. A small operational pilot can establish feasibility; it cannot by itself prove comparative superiority.
+
+## Sequence and timing judgment
+
+Start P01–P04 and P11 in parallel with named owners. Follow with the exact personal-check/release/decision chain while remaining L03/source/rule work continues. P02/P12 control infrastructure activation; P06–P10 plus independent review control personal-choice activation. P13 controls external action, not access to otherwise supported self-service education.
+
+The existing November 5 target belongs to the scoped infrastructure program. It is not a credible implied date for all fifteen company capabilities, full L03, consumer acceptance and enrollment. Estimate remaining effort after the whole-offering pilot measures actual reconciliation/review throughput and the clean-clone/restore exercise exposes integration work. A precise calendar promise before those measurements would be misleading.
