+      "trigger": "Identify the actual history-dependent finding/action and minimum rule-relevant period/eligibility anchor first; its actual Medicare-drug or other creditable-insurance history remains incomplete after reuse. Explain the consequence and ask only whether an interruption occurred, or only missing dates if already reported. Do not demand lifetime history or user day-count arithmetic, and do not ask because a notice was selected.",
+      "acceptable_evidence_or_confirmation": "Explicit no-interruption statement for a named relevant period or prior drug-insurance end/replacement start dates with beneficiary, policy, creditability period and provenance. One reply can supply both notice meaning and continuity. Reuse RC11 dates only when explicitly also the same prescription insurance/date type; medical insurance end alone is insufficient. Preserve exact/partial/scheduled precision; collect only what the requested rule needs.",
