+      "requirement": "Conditional internal dependency check; suppress routine-intake asking and defer collection until an actual supported contribution-sensitive enrollment/timing decision needs the missing status. Assess necessity, intrusion, comprehension/document burden and added turns before wording the ask. A desired start month, current-work coverage or incomplete template field alone is insufficient. Legitimate timing work can still require the status before HSA use is volunteered; do not assume no contributions.",
+      "trigger": "First identify the concrete requested timing action/result, relevant beneficiary/period, how different contribution answers change that result/next step and whether collecting now can advance useful supported work. Reuse explicit adequately bound reports/evidence from chat rather than asking again. If external holds make further personal intake unhelpful, defer collection and retain the precise dependent limitation. Only a necessary missing status earns a contextual ask, with an evident purpose or one short clause, not a long explanation. Explicit no HSA/contributions for the relevant period skips asking; a current no alone cannot close a separately necessary prior-period check. RC05 B dates are neither a universal prerequisite nor actual A chronology. Unasked is unanswered/not required for this task with an explicit reason, never a fabricated no, user deferral or verified non-applicability.",
+      "acceptable_evidence_or_confirmation": "Explicit user report of contributions by the person, employer or another contributor, or explicit none for the relevant account/period; an adequately scoped payroll/benefits/account contribution summary can be reused. Preserve account owner, period, source/confirmation/revision and verified:false. Account identifiers, balance, full statements and amounts are unnecessary solely to answer this status question. A reply giving a contribution amount can supply yes without re-asking or collecting more amounts. Unknown/defer is valid but supplies no contribution finding.",
+      "unknown_conflict_handling": "Unknown/defer is never no. Having a high-deductible plan, account/card/balance or using saved money for bills does not establish new contributions. Neither self no nor an empty payroll deduction proves employer/other contributions absent. Preserve materially conflicting period reports and clarify only what the requested check needs. A spouse's separate HSA is distinct from the beneficiary's, even on family insurance. Current no does not prove no relevant past contributions. The single choice cannot encode contributor/account/period, contribution tax-year allocation, actual deposit dates or future stop plans; retain supplied bindings and explicit G02/G07 gaps. No unchanged-unknown retry.",
