+    "readiness.facts.RC15.value.choice": {
+      "decision_affected": "Internal disposition of a reported coverage event/notice for a requested personal Medigap purchase/change-rights check; no independent substantive eligibility finding.",
+      "requirement": "Conditional internal report disposition only when that actual rights task needs event review. Suppress the standalone broad question and details/none menu; preserve the existing ID/field. General education/path browsing requires no event intake.",
+      "trigger": "A supported requested Medigap purchase/change conclusion needs an event-based protection still unresolved after reusing state, relevant age/basis, actual B history and existing event/end-date reports. If another established applicable federal/state protection suffices for this conclusion, skip unnecessary event collection. Derive disposition from an explicit substantive event/no-known-event report without a second selection. Missing B/state/age facts stay linked to RC02/RC05/RC06, not a duplicate RC15 questionnaire; an external policy hold alone earns no new personal question.",
+      "acceptable_evidence_or_confirmation": "An explicit user event/notice description or explicit no-known-event statement, with person, policy, period, source/confirmation/revision. A sufficiently specific report from RC08/RC11/chat can establish reported details disposition; that does not confirm a legal qualifying event. Unknown/defer is accepted without supplying a disposition outcome. No requirement to possess or upload a letter solely for this internal field.",
+      "unknown_conflict_handling": "No known change/notice is not no purchase protection, and no letter is not no event. A blank/unasked/unknown is not none or verified non-applicability. Preserve known events if part of the history is uncertain and keep conflicting periods/policies distinct. Event-report presence is separate from legal relevance; do not default voluntary loss to no rights or a reported loss to guaranteed issue. Reuse B dates as dates only, never as an event report.",
+      "source_data_layer": "Existing customer-profile report/confirmation provenance; L11 Medigap rights, with L13 timing. Exact state, official history/notices and reviewed policy are needed for personal rights conclusions. This describes required evidence, not independent acceptance. Exact state/federal rights, dated coverage terms and relevant notice evidence remain separate. Medicare.gov When can I buy a Medigap policy and the official Choosing a Medigap Policy guide checked October 27 support the distinctions; this is no accepted personal L11 policy or automatic activation of legacy B-date research wording.",
+      "readiness_gate": "This internal choice independently unlocks no purchase-right, deadline, underwriting, price or recommendation claim. Only the unresolved event-dependent conclusion is held when event information is actually needed; keep other established protections and supported comparisons available. No-known-event is not a negative rights decision. Actual substantive event/date facts, reviewed L11/L13 rules, jurisdiction and independent evidence/release acceptance remain separate.",
