+      "requirement": "Conditional at a supported assistance-dependent result/help task, not routine intake or a universal program checklist. Narrow to the still-unknown program fact actually needed. Accurate personal pricing can require this status even without a volunteered cost concern; a lower-cost preference alone is no income/eligibility finding.",
+      "trigger": "Identify the beneficiary, relevant state/program where needed, target cost/eligibility period and exact result affected; reuse T05/RC18/chat reports and applicable sufficiently bound accepted evidence first. Ask only a missing assistance fact that can change the supported next result, such as current Extra Help for personal prescription pricing or state Part B help for that premium task. A program-related help request may open brief education before any assessment. No affordability label or broad Medicaid report automatically opens a full means test, SNP interview or repeated assistance menu. If external holds mean collection cannot advance useful work, defer and retain the specific limitation.",
+      "acceptable_evidence_or_confirmation": "Explicit relevant program name/state/period report, a sufficiently scoped benefits/award/plan summary, explicit none known or unknown/decline. Reuse every known positive; one reply may name several programs. Preserve person, program, period, source/confirmation/revision with verified:false for user reports. Initial existing-status collection needs no income/assets, account numbers, SSN or full documents. An accepted rule may derive a linked entitlement from sufficiently established exact program facts, but label that derivation/source separately and never fabricate a customer confirmation of another program.",
