+      "trigger": "A broad military/veterans category or ambiguous current-program report still leaves a consequential program distinction unresolved after reuse. General education or a known program/rule needing no subtype skips it. I served in the military alone is not a current coverage report; ask only actual current program if material. Narrow the unselected program dropdown to relevant unresolved options and support typed/another/unknown/defer/help. Original RC04/RC12 dependencies do not require A/B or creditability interviews before naming a program; those facts are independently conditional to the actual subsequent rule. Missing external policy/source evidence earns no repeated program ask.",
+      "acceptable_evidence_or_confirmation": "Explicit program name(s) in T05/chat, clear option selection(s), typed beneficiary program description or confirmation of a consequential interpretation, with beneficiary/current versus past/pending status, period and original report/confirmation/revision. A current sufficiently specific named VA health care or TRICARE For Life report needs no second question/echo. Preserve multiple reported programs and partial knowledge. No member number, service record, rank, disability rating, proof upload or account access is needed just to identify the reported program. Help is an action, not a program answer.",
+      "unknown_conflict_handling": "Do not equate VA health care, TRICARE For Life, other TRICARE or CHAMPVA. Do not infer TFL solely from age/A-B/military history, attribute a spouse's/helper's benefits to the beneficiary, or treat planned/eligible coverage as active. Broad TRICARE can remain known while subtype is unknown. Unknown/defer/decline is not no coverage; preserve known positives alongside another uncertain program and typed Other. More-than-one reports may be compatible or need a narrow same-person/period clarification under actual official rules; never erase or auto-approve. The single choice cannot faithfully encode every combination, subtype, currentness or mixed uncertainty; retain G04/G13/G14 gaps and raw reports. No diagnosis, entitlement, general payer order or permission to cancel/change coverage is inferred.",
