+      "decision_affected": "Correct or resolve the exact reported fact/interpretation needed by a dependent result while preserving beneficiary, time, item, meaning and revision; no standalone coverage interview.",
+      "requirement": "Conditional internal integrity/correction check across the conversation. A consumer clarification is necessary only when the actual consequential correction/meaning remains unresolved; no universal closing confirmation, repeated question or required screen.",
+      "trigger": "First inspect original report, person/period/scope, prior confirmations and source/result binding. If two consequential reports genuinely disagree about the same fact or a consequential new interpretation remains unconfirmed, ask a named, contextual clarification. Different people, actual versus desired dates, past/future periods, or A/B enrollment versus Advantage benefit delivery are not automatically conflicts. A clear explicit correction already supplies the answer: update the actual reported fact and acknowledge without asking again. A wrong/stale plan/year/source or generated-result error is a system/evidence issue to investigate, not a reason to make the person repeat known facts. Use relevant unselected options/date/text plus another/unknown/defer only when needed.",
+      "acceptable_evidence_or_confirmation": "Explicit correction with unambiguous target/replacement or response confirming the named fact/interpretation, retaining original and replacement report, beneficiary/item/period, actor/source/confirmation/revision and relevant date precision. Reuse existing consequential confirmation instead of replaying RC28. Update the real T04/T05/provider/drug/budget/other supported field; choice is only correction disposition and cannot store the corrected value by itself. Do not invent target bindings when representation is insufficient; preserve G14. Corrected reports remain verified:false unless independently verified evidence separately supports the actual claim.",
+      "unknown_conflict_handling": "Unknown/defer/Neither does not select a preferred fact or mean no coverage. They apply at different times needs actual period binding before time-dependent findings; it is not permission to guess dates. Do not choose most recent/likely/nearest merely because it looks plausible. Distinguish an explicit correction that supersedes an old report from an unresolved new conflict; retain history rather than leave superseded reports as active contradictions. No global reset or unrelated re-asks. User confirmation cannot erase contrary external evidence or turn a disputed source result into verified coverage. Original Medicare/Advantage response choices cannot encode arbitrary dates/names/products or full current coverage; retain original reports and G04/G13/G14 gaps instead of forcing them.",
+      "source_data_layer": "Existing customer-profile report/confirmation provenance; original and corrected customer reports plus actual target-field/item/person/period and source/confirmation/revision provenance; exact domain/source evidence for any dependent external claim. Check source version/year/identity and interpretation errors before asking. Medicare.gov health-plan guidance checked October 27 supports distinguishing Part A/B entitlement from the way benefits are received; no automatic Original/Advantage conflict from A/B alone. Correction confirmation is not independent benefit verification, personal eligibility or acceptance of an external source. This describes required evidence, not independent acceptance.",
+      "readiness_gate": "Hold only results actually depending on the unresolved fact, or a comprehensive claim including it; unrelated supported work continues. A clear correction updates the target report and marks affected old findings stale/recomputes dependencies with provenance, including newly applicable conditional questions, without treating them as answered. The original empty staleOnChange list cannot preserve an outdated dependent finding. Repeat user confirmation only for a genuinely new consequential interpretation; independent verification remains required by the exact external claim and is never replaced by a corrected report. Neither choice nor complete reported correction releases recommendation, policy/source or personal coverage gates.",
+      "field_role": "correction_disposition",
+      "known_fact_links": [
+        "the exact original field/report/item/beneficiary/period being corrected",
+        "explicit user correction and already-confirmed intended meaning",
+        "existing T04/T05/T06/T07/T08/RC25/RC27 or other specific affected report with source/revision lineage",
+        "the actual source/result binding and version when the apparent conflict comes from a generated result"
+      ],
+      "question_ids": [
+        "RC28"
+      ],
