+      "requirement": "Conditional only when the requested comparison/action depends on consequences for known group-related benefits. No universal household question or automatic follow-up from RC12/RC09; basic education, published plan browsing and unaffected checks continue.",
+      "trigger": "T05/RC09/chat establishes the named group/retiree coverage and a concrete contemplated action, such as adding outside MA/PDP or leaving group insurance. Explain the consequence in simple language naming the known spouse/child/person and change, with only a relevant short example: does the wife/child keep work insurance if the person leaves that plan, or do both spouses keep work insurance if one adds Medicare drug coverage? Reuse a relevant confirmation already reported, then ask only the missing plan-specific effect. Examples imply no automatic loss and open no extra family interview. RC12 creditability, retirement or a spouse's existence alone does not trigger it. No relevant connected policy/action means explicit not-applicable reason rather than an assumed no effect.",
+      "acceptable_evidence_or_confirmation": "Explicit user report of what the actual plan/benefits administrator confirmed, or relevant policy/notice wording, tied to beneficiary, policy, exact proposed action, affected relationship/benefits and period. Minimal relevant passage or summary suffices for reported input; no family names/member numbers/full document. Record yes/no as the reported impact, with confirmation/source/revision provenance and verified:false. Reuse a sufficiently specific prior reply; not-checked/unknown/deferred is a valid response, not evidence of the outcome.",
+      "unknown_conflict_handling": "Unchecked/unknown/deferred/administrator unsure never becomes no effect. A user's expectation, creditable status, employer size, active-work status or only being the sole insured does not establish all plan-specific consequences. Preserve conflicting statements by policy/action/period and ask only a material clarification. One choice cannot encode what changes, who is affected, dates, re-entry conditions or mixed outcomes; retain available original report/evidence bindings and explicit G04/representation gaps, with no fabricated details or forced closest value. Recheck changed policy/action/period, without retrying an unchanged unknown.",
+      "source_data_layer": "Existing customer-profile report/confirmation provenance; L13 enrollment/coordination. Official enrollment/administrator notices and reviewed rule versions are separate from a user report. This describes required evidence, not independent acceptance. Exact employer/union/retiree benefit terms and dated administrator confirmation for this action/period remain separate from general Medicare rules and published MA benefit records. Medicare.gov creditable-coverage guidance checked October 27 supports possible group/family coverage impacts, not a personal determination. Relevant policy/action binding remains G04; no new source acceptance is implied.",
+      "readiness_gate": "Missing required consequence holds only claims that this action preserves existing benefits, has no household impact or is an established suitable transition. Keep otherwise supported comparisons with explicit limitations. An impact report does not automatically exclude a route or prove cancellation permission, eligibility, enrollment timing or re-entry rights. Explain the precise open finding, offer optional practical help, accept unknown/defer and continue unaffected work. Independent plan evidence, reviewed policy and release gates remain; generic yes/no alone cannot unlock recommendations.",
